Notebook[{
Cell["The High-Temperature Lindblad Limit of Caldeira-Leggett", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell["\<\
Keeping one term past white noise turns the non-positive Caldeira-Leggett \
master equation into a guaranteed Lindblad generator; carrying the \
fluctuation-path expansion to all orders reveals its Bernoulli-number \
structure and why exactly two terms are special. Worked out and verified with \
the Wolfram Language.\
\>", "Subtitle",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami (last updated: August 17, 2026)", "Author",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["Wolfram Research Inc, USA", "Affiliation",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The textbook high-temperature limit of quantum Brownian motion collapses \
the Feynman-Vernon decoherence kernel to white noise, and the resulting \
Caldeira-Leggett master equation is famously not completely positive: its \
Kossakowski matrix carries a negative eigenvalue. Following Pleasance, Aurell \
and Petruccione (arXiv:2508.14262), this essay treats the kernel as a \
tempered distribution and keeps exactly one term past white noise, a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],
 " piece whose weight is fixed by the single integral ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[Infinity]",
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sinh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], "/", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],
 ". That one term fills the momentum slot the standard treatment leaves \
empty, lifts the Kossakowski determinant from negative to positive, and does \
so with a generator that is completely independent of the ultraviolet cutoff ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],
 ". We build the kernel algebra from primitives, assemble the Kossakowski \
matrix and read its spectrum, then watch the correction rescue positivity \
dynamically: for a quadratic potential the master equation closes on the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 " covariance, and a position-squeezed state that pierces the Robertson-Schr\
\[ODoubleDot]dinger uncertainty floor under Caldeira-Leggett stays above it \
once the new term is present. Carrying the fluctuation-path expansion to all \
orders, we find its coefficients are the Bernoulli numbers and that the whole \
tower resums to the exact Ohmic kernel; the first higher term, a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],
 ", carries a potential-dependent operator that leaves the two-operator \
Lindblad family and is anti-diffusive because the next Bernoulli number is \
negative, yet for a harmonic potential it sharpens the agreement with the \
quantum Gibbs state from order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],
 " to order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "4"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 ", and the expansion converges down to the first Matsubara frequency, where \
the bath memory turns genuinely non-Markovian."
}], "Abstract",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],

Cell["Setting the Stage: How This Notebook Flows", "Subsection",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook is a computation-first tour of one idea in open quantum \
systems: the correct Markovian limit of the Caldeira-Leggett model of quantum \
Brownian motion. We start from the Feynman-Vernon influence functional and \
its decoherence kernel, watch the standard high-temperature limit throw that \
kernel down to white noise, and then recover the one term it discards by \
treating the kernel as a tempered distribution rather than an ordinary \
function. From that single correction we assemble the Markovian generator, \
read its Kossakowski matrix to decide whether it is a legitimate Lindblad \
generator, and, for a harmonic potential, reduce the whole master equation to \
a drift-plus-diffusion flow of the covariance matrix and watch positivity be \
lost or saved in a single plot. The last stretch goes past the paper: it \
carries the fluctuation-path expansion to all orders, resums it into the \
exact kernel, and asks what the higher terms do to the operator content, to \
positivity, and to how far down in temperature the master equation can reach.\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In other words, I have tried to build a catalogue of computational \
experiments around one paper's central claim, so that every abstract \
statement about positivity and cutoff-independence is something you can \
evaluate, perturb, and see for yourself. I strongly believe in a \
computation-first narrative for learning: in a sense, if I cannot compute it, \
I cannot claim to understand it. Here that conviction has teeth, because the \
entire dispute between the standard master equation and the corrected one is \
settled by the sign of a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 " determinant and by whether one curve dips below zero."
}], "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The environment you see is a live Wolfram notebook. Evaluate the cells from \
top to bottom. I kept the symbolic parameters ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["M", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],
 " genuinely symbolic throughout the algebra, and only substituted numbers \
where a plot demands them, so most cells return closed forms you can inspect. \
Some later cells reuse definitions from earlier ones, so be mindful of \
order."
}], "Text",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],

Cell["\<\
The story is presented as a continuous sequence, like a movie. I have added \
headings to help with transitions, but the narrative runs straight through: \
concept, then computation, then interpretation. Some code will look dense at \
first. My suggestion is to read the output and its meaning before worrying \
about every detail of the input, then go back and unpack the code once you \
know what it produced. And remember that you are not locked into the code as \
given: change the temperature, change the squeezing, add the cross-diffusion \
term, and watch the verdict move.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],

Cell["Prerequisites and How to Read This", "Subsection",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],

Cell["\<\
This tour is self-contained but moves at the pace of a research paper. It \
assumes comfort with the density-operator description of open systems, the \
Lindblad (GKSL) form of a Markovian master equation, canonical commutators, \
and a little distribution theory (the Dirac delta and its derivatives as \
tempered distributions). The final part uses the covariance-matrix \
description of Gaussian states and the Lyapunov equation for its steady \
state; both are built up here from the moment equations, so no prior exposure \
is strictly required, though the pace there is steeper.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],

Cell["Let's start!", "Text",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],

Cell["\<\
Part I: The Caldeira-Leggett Model and the Feynman-Vernon Kernel\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Fix the object of study. A quantum particle of mass ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["M", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],
 ", position ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],
 ", momentum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 ", moving in a potential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],
 ", is coupled bilinearly to a bath of harmonic oscillators held at \
temperature ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 " (write ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"], "=", "1", "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],
 "). The total Hamiltonian is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["I", "TI"]], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["C", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],
 ", with system Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], "2"], "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],
 ", bath ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "=", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], "2"], "/", "2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], "2"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],
 ", bilinear coupling ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["I", "TI"]], "=", "-", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],
 ", and a counter-term ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],
 " that keeps the Hamiltonian translation-invariant. This is the \
Caldeira-Leggett model, the workhorse of quantum Brownian motion."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Integrating out the bath under a path-integral treatment leaves the reduced \
dynamics of the particle governed by the Feynman-Vernon influence functional ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalF]", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[Prime]"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["exp",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "-", 
    FractionBox["1", "\[HBar]"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],
 ", a double integral over a forward path ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],
 " and a backward path ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[Prime]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 ". The imaginary part ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],
 " is dissipation (friction); the real part ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],
 " is decoherence, and it is the one with memory. Writing the paths in terms \
of the fluctuation coordinate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[Prime]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],
 ", the decoherence action is"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["f", "TI"]],
     LimitsPositioning->False], "\[NegativeThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], "\[NegativeThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], "\[ThickSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "-", 
     StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "so the entire memory of decoherence lives in one object, the real kernel ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],
 ". Equivalently, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 " is the force-force correlation function of a classical Gaussian noise with \
which the bath is, for the purpose of decoherence, indistinguishable. \
Everything in this essay is a statement about this one function."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1589986527,ExpressionUUID->"134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For an Ohmic bath with spectral density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "-", 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],
 ", cut off at the ultraviolet frequency ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],
 ", the kernel is the cosine transform of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["coth",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "/", "2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}], "\[Pi]"], 
    UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[CapitalOmega]",
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "\[ThickSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["coth",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[NegativeThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["(",
     FontSize->1.8 Inherited], 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
      StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], 
    StyleBox[")",
     FontSize->1.8 Inherited], 
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two scales sit inside this integral: the cutoff ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 ", which limits the bath's response time, and the thermal time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "=", "\[HBar]", "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],
 ", which limits the range of the memory. The whole paper is about what \
happens to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],
 " when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["B", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],
 " is small but not zero."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],

Cell["\<\
Define the thermal weight and look at its small-argument behavior, since that \
is where the high-temperature limit lives:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", "\[Omega]", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Coth", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Omega]", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["coth",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "/", "2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],
 " at leading order, a constant independent of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],
 ", with the first correction quadratic in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],
 ". The leading constant is the classical equipartition value, and it is the \
term the standard high-temperature limit keeps. The quadratic correction is \
the term this essay is about."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],

Cell["\<\
Part II: The Standard High-Temperature Limit: White Noise, and What It \
Discards\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The textbook move is to send ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],
 " and keep only the leading term of the thermal weight. Concretely, replace ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["coth",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
    StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "/", "2"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],
 " by its small-argument value."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1653200050,ExpressionUUID->"2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],

Cell["\<\
Expand the hyperbolic cotangent for small argument, which is the substitution \
the standard limit makes:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Coth", "[", 
    RowBox[{"x", "/", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->519689844,ExpressionUUID->"46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["coth",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "/", "2"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "2", "/", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "/", "6", "-", "\[Ellipsis]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],
 ". Keeping only the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "/", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
 " term is exactly the white-noise approximation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["coth",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
    StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "/", "2"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\[TildeTilde]", "2", "/", "\[HBar]", 
   StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],
 ". Notice the very next term, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "/", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],
 ": it is small, it is usually thrown away, and it is the entire subject of \
the correction we will recover. The standard limit does not merely \
approximate the kernel; it discards a specific term whose fingerprint we can \
track."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1609367578,ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With only the leading term, the kernel becomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\[TildeTilde]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "/", "\[Pi]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[CapitalOmega]",
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "/", "\[Pi]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],
 ". As the cutoff is removed, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],
 " is a nascent Dirac delta."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1541450781,ExpressionUUID->"48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Confirm that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "\[Pi]", 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],
 " carries unit area, so it converges to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],
 " as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "\[Rule]", "\[Infinity]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", " ", "\[Tau]"}], "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"Pi", " ", "\[Tau]"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Tau]", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"-", "Infinity"}], ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
   "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->1140508347,ExpressionUUID->"3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the area is exactly one, independent of ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],
 ", so the finite-cutoff kernel collapses to the singular white-noise kernel"
}], "Text",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"4", 
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["B", "TI"]]], " ", 
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This memoryless kernel is what produces the standard Caldeira-Leggett \
master equation. We will see in Part IV that it is precisely one term short \
of positivity. Recovering the missing term is a matter of not discarding the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "/", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],
 " we just watched go by."
}], "Text",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Part III: The Kernel as a Tempered Distribution: The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["sinh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "2"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],
 " Form and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],
 " Correction"
}], "Section",
 CellID->203008389,ExpressionUUID->"1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The key methodological choice is to treat ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],
 " not as an ordinary function but as a tempered distribution, an object that \
only ever appears smeared against a smooth test function. The paper's central \
representation of the Ohmic kernel, valid up to corrections that vanish as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "\[Rule]", "\[Infinity]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],
 ", is"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1090263105,ExpressionUUID->"5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}], "\[Pi]"], "[", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     FractionBox[
      SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["B", "TI"], "2"]], " ", 
     FractionBox["1", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["sinh",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{"\[Pi]", 
        StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "/", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["B", "TI"]]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "+", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], " ", 
     StyleBox["O", "TI"], "\[NegativeThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["(",
      FontSize->1.8 Inherited], 
     FractionBox["1", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", 
         StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], "3"]], 
     StyleBox[")",
      FontSize->1.8 Inherited]}], "]"}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1560876240,ExpressionUUID->"07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "a hyperbolic-cosecant-squared profile whose width is set by the thermal \
time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["B", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],
 ", plus a remainder controlled entirely by the cutoff. Let us reconstruct \
the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["sinh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "2"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],
 " core from primitives, following Sec. I of the Supplemental Material, then \
extract the correction the white-noise limit dropped."
}], "Text",
 CellID->176337227,ExpressionUUID->"6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The kernel is a second derivative of a simpler thermal primitive. Compute \
the thermal part of that primitive, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"t", "h"}], "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[Infinity]",
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["coth",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], "-", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],
 ", where subtracting the ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],
 " isolates the thermal from the vacuum contribution:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->807053435,ExpressionUUID->"5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Coth", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x", "/", "2"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
     RowBox[{"s", " ", "x"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"s", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->1633675818,ExpressionUUID->"30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the thermal primitive is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"t", "h"}], "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "\[Pi]", 
   StyleBox["coth",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Pi]", 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "-", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],
 ", a closed form. The physics of the thermal weight has been packed into a \
single hyperbolic cotangent."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1828793009,ExpressionUUID->"323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Differentiate the primitive once more to reach the kernel itself, since the \
Feynman-Vernon kernel is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["G", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1232986364,ExpressionUUID->"511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"D", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Pi", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Coth", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Pi", " ", "s"}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "s"}]}], ",", " ", "s"}], "]"}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "Simplify"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->762269937,ExpressionUUID->"36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the derivative is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sinh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],
 ". The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],
 " is a vacuum term that cancels against the vacuum part of the primitive; \
the surviving thermal piece is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sinh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],
 ", which is exactly the profile quoted above. So the kernel really is a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["sinh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "2"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],
 ", and this is the function we must now integrate against the paths."
}], "Text",
 CellID->405213039,ExpressionUUID->"12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here is the subtlety that makes the whole construction work, and the reason \
the kernel must be handled as a distribution. The memory kernel ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], "/", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sinh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "/", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],
 " behaves like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],
 " near the origin, so it is not integrable there. Cut the integral off at a \
lower limit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[CurlyEpsilon]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],
 " and integrate the tail:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2118931930,ExpressionUUID->"65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Csch", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Pi", " ", "s"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "\[Epsilon]", ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Epsilon]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->1039057480,ExpressionUUID->"5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The tail integral is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["coth",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Pi]", 
    StyleBox["\[CurlyEpsilon]", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],
 ", finite for any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[CurlyEpsilon]", "TI"], ">", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],
 ". Now let the lower limit approach the origin:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1411198270,ExpressionUUID->"1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Coth", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Pi", " ", "\[Epsilon]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "Pi"}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Epsilon]", " ", "->", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Direction", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<FromAbove\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->1703453532,ExpressionUUID->"187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],

Cell["\<\
As one can see, it runs off to infinity: a naive numerical integration of the \
bare kernel would diverge here, and the object is only meaningful as a \
distribution.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1477609488,ExpressionUUID->"641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The regularization is the one distribution theory prescribes: subtract the \
value of the test function at the origin. The decoherence functional, after \
the integration by parts of Sec. II of the Supplemental Material, reduces to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["F", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "2", "\[Pi]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", "\[Pi]", 
   UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[Infinity]",
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sinh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "2"}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],
 ", where the subtraction ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],
 " tames the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],
 " singularity because a smooth even test function has ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],
 ". Confirm that the subtracted integral is finite by evaluating it against a \
concrete even test function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1030824397,ExpressionUUID->"7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Csch", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Pi", " ", "s"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
       RowBox[{"k", " ", "s"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"k", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->100031176,ExpressionUUID->"3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the subtracted integral is the finite closed form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", "-", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["coth",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], "/", "2"}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],
 ". The lesson to carry forward is a rule of practice: integrate the \
subtracted integrand ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sinh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "2"}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],
 ", never the bare kernel."
}], "Text",
 CellID->144223354,ExpressionUUID->"51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now expand the subtraction to lowest order to read off the correction. For \
a smooth even test function, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\[TildeTilde]", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],
 ", so the leading correction is weighted by the second moment of the kernel. \
Compute that moment, the single integral that fixes the size of the whole \
correction:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1443527617,ExpressionUUID->"0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"x", "^", "2"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Csch", "[", "x", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->311511756,ExpressionUUID->"7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[Infinity]",
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sinh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], "/", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],
 ". This one number, the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], "/", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],
 " that appears in the Basel problem, sets the weight of the term the \
white-noise limit discarded. In the variables of the kernel the same moment \
reads ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[Infinity]",
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sinh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "2"}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], "2"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "=", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"6", "\[Pi]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1381425643,ExpressionUUID->"2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Csch", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Pi", " ", "s"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"s", "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->377280352,ExpressionUUID->"7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify that the two computations agree by expanding the subtracted \
test-function integral at small ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],
 ", which isolates the same second moment:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1717363484,ExpressionUUID->"6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"k", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Coth", "[", 
         RowBox[{"k", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}]}], ")"}], "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "//", 
  " ", "Normal"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->1781880651,ExpressionUUID->"6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the small-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],
 " expansion is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"12", "\[Pi]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],
 ", which is exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],
 " times the second moment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"6", "\[Pi]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],
 ": the coefficient in front of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],
 " is fixed, and it is nonzero. Collecting the leading singular term and this \
correction, the kernel expanded one step past white noise is"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1536527082,ExpressionUUID->"289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[TildeTilde]", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"4", 
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["B", "TI"]]], " ", 
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["B", "TI"]]}], "3"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1621535814,ExpressionUUID->"12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first term is the standard white-noise kernel of Part II. The second \
term, proportional to the second derivative of the delta and to the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], "/", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],
 " moment, is the correction. It vanishes as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],
 ", so it is invisible in the strict high-temperature limit, but at any \
finite temperature it is present, and it is what the next part turns into a \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],
 " term in the master equation."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1193935837,ExpressionUUID->"01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One more closed form deserves its own cell, because it is the \
antiderivative that controls the boundary contributions to the action (Sec. \
III of the Supplemental Material). Compute ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sinh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],
 ", the running version of the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], "/", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],
 " moment:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->105329933,ExpressionUUID->"49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"x", "^", "2"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Csch", "[", "x", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "y"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"y", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->1234416869,ExpressionUUID->"2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],

Cell["\<\
Confirm that this antiderivative saturates at the moment we already found, so \
the boundary terms reach a finite plateau:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->240380995,ExpressionUUID->"0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"y", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"y", " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"y", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Coth", "[", "y", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Log", "[", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"E", "^", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "y"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], ")"}]}], 
    " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{"PolyLog", "[", 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"E", "^", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "y"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Pi", "^", "2"}], "/", "6"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"y", " ", "->", " ", "Infinity"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->1771870337,ExpressionUUID->"52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],
 " climbs from zero and levels off at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], "/", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],
 ", the polylogarithm ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Li",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "2", 
     StyleBox["y", "TI"]}]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],
 " carrying the approach to the plateau. The rate of that approach is set by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["B", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],
 ", so as the temperature rises the boundary contributions collapse onto the \
endpoints of the time interval and drop out, which is why the bulk correction \
above is the whole story at high temperature."
}], "Text",
 CellID->305160771,ExpressionUUID->"612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Visualize how quickly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],
 " reaches its plateau for a few thermal times, reproducing the behavior of \
Fig. 3 of the paper:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1896945989,ExpressionUUID->"296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"b", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", "tauB"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"y", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Pi", " ", 
            RowBox[{"tt", "/", "tauB"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"y", " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"y", " ", "-", " ", 
             RowBox[{"y", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Coth", "[", "y", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"2", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Log", "[", 
               RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
                RowBox[{"E", "^", 
                 RowBox[{"(", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "y"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
            ")"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PolyLog", "[", 
           RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"E", "^", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "y"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Pi", "^", "2"}], "/", "6"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
   ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Evaluate", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"b", "[", 
         RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "tauB"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"tauB", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
       "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<\[Tau]B = \>\"", ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", 
         "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], ")"}]}], ",",
      "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"AxesLabel", " ", "->", " ", "None"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<B(\[Pi] t/\[Tau]B)\>\""}], "}"}]}],
      ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
     "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<Boundary antiderivative saturates at \[Pi]^2/6\>\""}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"Dashed", ",", " ", "Gray", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Pi", "^", "2"}], "/", "6"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Pi", "^", "2"}], "/", "6"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}],
        "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "460"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->653417278,ExpressionUUID->"6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, a smaller thermal time reaches the plateau sooner, so at \
high temperature the deviation of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],
 " from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], "/", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],
 " is confined to a vanishing neighborhood of the endpoints. This is the \
computational content of the statement that the end terms are negligible."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1067269536,ExpressionUUID->"6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],

Cell["\<\
Part IV: From Kernel to Lindblad: The Kossakowski Matrix and Guaranteed \
Positivity\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->49659130,ExpressionUUID->"73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],

Cell["\<\
Now translate the kernel into a generator. Rewriting the influence functional \
in superoperator form turns the corrected kernel into a Markovian master \
equation for the reduced density operator, the Liouvillian\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->464508221,ExpressionUUID->"31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"], "=", "-", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["S", "TI"]], ",", 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[HBar]"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"], "}"}]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"]}], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"]}], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", "2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"]}], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1361313038,ExpressionUUID->"72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with friction coefficient ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],
 " and Dekker diffusion coefficients"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1907680634,ExpressionUUID->"106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"6", 
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
     SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{"0", "."}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->483148123,ExpressionUUID->"7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "These coefficients are not fresh inputs: they are what the two kernel terms \
of Part III become under the Feynman-Vernon to superoperator map (Aurell \
2020), which sends a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],
 " term of weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["w", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],
 " to a decoherence coefficient ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["w", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", "\[HBar]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],
 " on the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],
 " channel, and a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],
 " term of weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["w", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["w", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], "2"], "\[HBar]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],
 " on the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],
 " channel. Substitute the physical identifications ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "=", "\[HBar]", "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],
 " into the white-noise weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],
 " and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],
 " weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "/", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],
 ", and read off the two coefficients:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1195452142,ExpressionUUID->"160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"4", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Eta]", "/", "\[Tau]B"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[HBar]"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Tau]B", "/", "3"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
        RowBox[{"M", "^", "2"}], " ", "\[HBar]"}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}], "\n", 
   "   ", "/.", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"M", " ", "\[Gamma]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Tau]B", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->1521685512,ExpressionUUID->"10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the two weights land exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"6", 
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],
 ". The white-noise ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],
 " term is the standard position-decoherence coefficient of the old \
treatment; the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],
 " term, carrying the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], "/", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],
 " moment, is the new momentum-diffusion coefficient, and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],
 " that sets it apart is the pair of time derivatives in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],
 " turning position differences into momentum."
}], "Text",
 CellID->97201263,ExpressionUUID->"66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The single new object is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],
 ", the position-diffusion coefficient carried by the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],
 " double commutator. It is exactly the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],
 " correction of Part III, and in the standard Caldeira-Leggett treatment it \
is zero. Two facts are worth stating before any computation: this generator \
holds for any potential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],
 ", because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],
 " only shapes the free evolution and not the diffusion timescales, and every \
assembled coefficient is independent of the cutoff ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],
 ". That the finite-",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],
 " remainder of the kernel (the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], " ", 
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", 
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    RowBox[{"-", "3"}]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],
 " tail of Part III) drops out in the scaling limit is the paper's \
distributional argument; what we can check directly, against Table I below, \
is that no cutoff survives in the assembled coefficients."
}], "Text",
 CellID->878831761,ExpressionUUID->"63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Whether such a generator describes a legitimate quantum evolution is \
decided by one matrix. In Lindblad (GKSL) form the dissipator is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"], 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
     FractionBox["1", "2"], "{", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"], "}"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],
 ", and the dynamics is completely positive if and only if the Kossakowski \
matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],
 " is positive semidefinite. With the two Hermitian Lindblad operators ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], "1"], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], "2"], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],
 ", the diffusion coefficients and the friction assemble into a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],
 " matrix."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1048559713,ExpressionUUID->"54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],

Cell["\<\
Define the Kossakowski matrix as a function of the three Dekker coefficients, \
with the friction fixing the off-diagonal:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->300048012,ExpressionUUID->"6334ac9c-43f1-85c0-12cb-45c67585ef2a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "kossakowski", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"kossakowski", "[", 
    RowBox[{"dxx_", ",", " ", "dpp_", ",", " ", "dxp_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "dpp"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "dxp"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"I", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", "\[HBar]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "                                   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "dxp"}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"I", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", "\[HBar]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "dxx"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->1962937852,ExpressionUUID->"74397683-04f4-1d4d-1dc7-6fedac816797"],

Cell["\<\
Build the matrix for the coefficients of this work and display it:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->588230824,ExpressionUUID->"735e49d5-32a1-4a48-2166-609f47541892"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"kossakowski", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"6", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Gamma]", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", 
     RowBox[{"T", "/", 
      RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}]}]}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], " ", "//", 
  " ", "MatrixForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->2099309037,ExpressionUUID->"335d55a2-cf9b-493d-6163-4c0fea2e1807"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The diagonal carries the two diffusion coefficients and the off-diagonal \
carries the friction as a pure imaginary ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[MinusPlus]", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bfbbd45-edb8-1b0b-6998-352e844d6651"],
 ". The question of positivity is now the sign of a determinant."
}], "Text",
 CellID->512383039,ExpressionUUID->"045023ab-c37d-b770-2c6f-baf4f6091a5a"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the determinant of the Kossakowski matrix for this work:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->273308241,ExpressionUUID->"73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
   RowBox[{"kossakowski", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"6", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Gamma]", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", 
      RowBox[{"T", "/", 
       RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}]}]}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
  "//", " ", "FullSimplify"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->1809098798,ExpressionUUID->"33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the determinant is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"3", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],
 ", strictly positive. Positivity of a Kossakowski matrix is a statement \
about a Hermitian matrix, so confirm both that the matrix is Hermitian and \
that its two leading principal minors are positive, which is Sylvester's \
criterion for positive-definiteness, assuming the physical parameters are \
positive:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->156430199,ExpressionUUID->"167ebcf0-2b32-2a61-3e05-35ba4ec7794b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"kossakowski", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"6", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Gamma]", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", 
        RowBox[{"T", "/", 
         RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}]}]}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",",
    "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"a", " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "a", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"a", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Det", "[", "a", "]"}], " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"M", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"kB", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"T", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[19]:= ",
 CellID->724760089,ExpressionUUID->"15eb24b6-b946-3a65-43e8-bdf038f0894f"],

Cell["\<\
As one can see, the matrix is Hermitian and both leading principal minors are \
positive, so it is positive definite and the generator is genuinely Lindblad. \
Now set the position-diffusion coefficient to zero, which is the standard \
Caldeira-Leggett master equation, and recompute the determinant:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->168408080,ExpressionUUID->"27d2a24c-1e84-19ee-4de1-44169b316b34"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
   RowBox[{"kossakowski", "[", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Gamma]", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", 
      RowBox[{"T", "/", 
       RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}]}]}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
  "//", " ", "FullSimplify"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:= ",
 CellID->811283638,ExpressionUUID->"285985c7-a1c8-13eb-5866-1ca0d07d6131"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the determinant is now ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57868ed1-450c-c474-7dbd-279b6cbeaf5e"],
 ", strictly negative. A negative determinant of a Hermitian matrix means one \
eigenvalue is negative, so the Caldeira-Leggett generator is not completely \
positive. This is the discrepancy the paper resolves: the missing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c5e608e-35dc-f74f-3466-79e8bc6edd95"],
 " term is exactly what the sign of this determinant is waiting for."
}], "Text",
 CellID->207978548,ExpressionUUID->"1a1e4090-3303-05ed-4a26-59da46b66f37"],

Cell["\<\
Assemble the comparison that the paper presents as Table I, computing each \
generator's determinant symbolically and reading its Lindblad verdict:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->437474228,ExpressionUUID->"10256af3-3972-af7a-41da-83bdb804f240"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "detA", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"detA", "[", 
    RowBox[{"dxx_", ",", " ", "dxp_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
     RowBox[{"kossakowski", "[", 
      RowBox[{"dxx", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Gamma]", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", 
        RowBox[{"T", "/", 
         RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}]}]}], ",", " ", "dxp"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
    " ", "//", " ", "FullSimplify"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Grid", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<master equation\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<det a\>\"", ",", 
       " ", "\"\<Lindblad\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<This work\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"detA", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"6", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
         "0"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<yes\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Di\[OAcute]si\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"detA", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"6", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"6", " ", "Pi", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}]}]}], "]"}],
        ",", " ", "\"\<yes\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Breuer-Petruccione\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"detA", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"8", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "\[Gamma]"}], " ", "kB", " ", 
          RowBox[{"T", "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}], " ", "\[CapitalOmega]"}], 
            ")"}]}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<marginal\>\""}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Caldeira-Leggett\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"detA", "[", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<no\>\""}], 
      "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Alignment", " ", "->", " ", "Left"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:= ",
 CellID->874582697,ExpressionUUID->"457602f1-d86e-ac86-730d-9bbad918f6ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the four rows separate cleanly by the sign of a single \
determinant. This work is positive. The Di",
 "[",
 "OAcute]si determinant is positive in its stated regime ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[GreaterEqual]", "\[HBar]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "499f95c1-a958-6c18-7fa4-0caac8ed3762"],
 ", since the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f1e874b-6d22-b8ab-3525-1f1504d40af1"],
 " subtraction stays below the leading ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"3", "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c02104f-9807-e6c4-3431-8a2919b3cc2e"],
 ". The Breuer-Petruccione determinant is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "4", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "4"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f909018-5ea1-6a32-15af-0a425b543918"],
 ", negative for finite ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f4595f3-090a-1216-557a-0cbda8bf617c"],
 " and only marginally positive as its cross-diffusion is dropped, which is \
the approximation its authors note. And Caldeira-Leggett is negative. Notice \
the columns for the other three all contain the cutoff ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06385f5e-e9d4-4e6c-2fd8-571b886114b6"],
 "; only this work's determinant is free of it."
}], "Text",
 CellID->11631581,ExpressionUUID->"25d2fb85-296f-82e5-53e1-f2ef481bd0cf"],

Cell["\<\
Make that observation literal. Collect this work's two nonzero coefficients \
alongside the cross-diffusion terms that Di[OAcute]si and Breuer-Petruccione \
carry, and test each for freedom from the cutoff:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1933762060,ExpressionUUID->"3b9a140e-d97a-4136-69b9-8e6bd80f101c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"FreeQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "\[CapitalOmega]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
  " ", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"6", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Gamma]", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", 
     RowBox[{"T", "/", 
      RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"6", " ", "Pi", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "\[Gamma]"}], " ", "kB", " ", 
     RowBox[{"T", "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}], " ", "\[CapitalOmega]"}], ")"}]}]}]}], 
   "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:= ",
 CellID->1055776787,ExpressionUUID->"4f9438da-b80f-a114-75ab-b18439bbf07e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, this work's coefficients are free of the cutoff while both \
other cross-diffusion terms retain it. Keeping the next term of the kernel is \
exactly what lets ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "\[Rule]", "\[Infinity]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7281c19b-2602-dcd4-22be-d8c553b4a63e"],
 " be taken at fixed temperature, so the cutoff leaves no trace in the \
assembled generator, which is the sense in which this is the genuinely \
cutoff-free Markovian limit."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1859711813,ExpressionUUID->"3c8746fc-db76-c487-64bd-5fb9de00aeed"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Before leaving the matrix, verify that it really does encode the generator \
we wrote down, not just a matrix with a convenient determinant. This check \
and the covariance cross-check in Part V both need the same ingredients: the \
position and momentum operators of a truncated harmonic oscillator, built \
from the annihilation matrix, together with the commutator and anticommutator \
as plain functions (neither the built-in ",
 Cell[BoxData["Commutator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11f0f87a-e6f0-91cd-478f-f227928ae317"],
 " nor ",
 Cell[BoxData["Anticommutator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "473164ce-b547-c1f4-6ecf-7da83cf393de"],
 " reduces on explicit matrices, both staying as an inert ",
 Cell[BoxData["NonCommutativeMultiply"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12c4fc3b-e00c-2bba-42fb-f66491b97980"],
 ", so we build ",
 Cell[BoxData["Dot"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7e6892-18cd-6f45-4b05-81dc997835af"],
 "-based versions). Define them once, and confirm the operators satisfy the \
canonical commutator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "325c8f47-cd85-89da-6263-2720e431db20"],
 " away from the top of the truncation:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1348896709,ExpressionUUID->"43fcea2e-12ab-c026-7183-0388a75f930c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"comm", ",", " ", "acomm", ",", " ", "oscillatorOps"}], "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
    RowBox[{"u_", ",", " ", "v_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"u", " ", ".", " ", "v"}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{"v", " ", ".", " ", "u"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"acomm", "[", 
    RowBox[{"u_", ",", " ", "v_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"u", " ", ".", " ", "v"}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{"v", " ", ".", " ", "u"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"oscillatorOps", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "hbar_", ",", " ", "mm_", ",", " ", "w0_"}], 
    "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"SparseArray", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Band", "[", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
             RowBox[{"n", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       
       RowBox[{"x0", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", "mm", " ", "w0"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"p0", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"hbar", " ", "mm", " ", 
          RowBox[{"w0", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x0", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"a", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "a", "]"}]}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"I", " ", "p0", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "a", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "a"}], 
         ")"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"xp", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"oscillatorOps", "[", 
      RowBox[{"8", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], 
    "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"comm", " ", "@@", " ", "xp"}], ")"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "5"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "5"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"I", " ", 
      RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "5", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[23]:= ",
 CellID->1427211115,ExpressionUUID->"5b416c07-c3d3-bf4f-097e-8660f6670595"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, on the retained subspace the commutator equals ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5add4728-e92e-eff1-0ae3-5f7588d8b5db"],
 " (here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "621761a3-d300-b412-122d-780ce6ba1f78"],
 "): the zero matrix shown is its difference from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], " ", "\|01d7d9"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b08d465-1dcc-fb87-0937-ce4f947ec9ed"],
 ". The one place this fails is the last row of the truncation, where the \
coupling to the discarded level ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d3ffb2e-09a8-fc78-24c4-f288a842c742"],
 " is missing, which is why every numerical check below reads its moments \
from random states supported well below the cutoff, where the operators are \
canonical."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2099805207,ExpressionUUID->"4139b36b-52b1-2977-70c6-2b356744785d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now assemble the GKSL dissipator from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "494d6e39-7750-b6eb-7f72-806302ea1c31"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], "1"], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39b01e29-d171-5c92-6f4f-9072e00426f8"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], "2"], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f6d713e-2461-11c8-7513-69784d146312"],
 ", and compare it to the double-commutator Liouvillian acting on a random \
density matrix:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1402006442,ExpressionUUID->"14ad582f-66ff-93eb-3c53-5189128be131"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", "50"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"hbar", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"mm", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"w0", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "10"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"kt", " ", "=", " ", "5"}], ",", " ", "xop", ",", " ", "pop", ",",
      " ", "ls", ",", " ", "amat", ",", " ", "dpp", ",", " ", "dxx", ",", " ",
      "gksl", ",", " ", "dekker", ",", " ", "lamb", ",", " ", "rho", ",", " ",
      "blk"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"xop", ",", " ", "pop"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"oscillatorOps", "[", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "hbar", ",", " ", "mm", ",", " ", "w0"}], 
      "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"dpp", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "gam", " ", "mm", " ", 
      RowBox[{"kt", "/", 
       RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}]}]}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"dxx", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"6", " ", "mm", " ", "kt"}], ")"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"ls", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"xop", ",", " ", "pop"}], "}"}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"amat", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "dpp"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"gam", "/", "hbar"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"I", " ", 
          RowBox[{"gam", "/", "hbar"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "dxx"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gksl", "[", "r_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"amat", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "j"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"ls", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "i", "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "r", " ", ".", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", 
            RowBox[{"ls", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", "j", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "\n", "       ", "-", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"acomm", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", 
               RowBox[{"ls", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", "j", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
              RowBox[{"ls", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", "i", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]}]}], 
         ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"dekker", "[", "r_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"gam", "/", "hbar"}], ")"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"xop", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"acomm", "[", 
          RowBox[{"pop", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"dpp", " ", 
       RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"xop", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
          RowBox[{"xop", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", "       ", "-",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{"dxx", " ", 
       RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"pop", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
          RowBox[{"pop", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"lamb", "[", "r_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"I", " ", 
        RowBox[{"gam", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "hbar"}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"acomm", "[", 
         RowBox[{"xop", ",", " ", "pop"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]}]}], 
    ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "7", "]"}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"blk", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"RandomComplex", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "1"}], " ", "-", " ", "I"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", "I"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"12", ",", " ", "12"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"blk", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"blk", " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "blk", "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"SparseArray", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      "0."}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"rho", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "12"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "12"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
     "blk"}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"rho", "/", 
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "rho", "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
     RowBox[{"Abs", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"gksl", "[", "rho", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"dekker", "[", "rho", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"lamb", "[", "rho", "]"}]}], ")"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "20"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "20"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[24]:= ",
 CellID->1901179466,ExpressionUUID->"4f7ea056-2d28-85ec-7505-3a1044c2ef36"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the GKSL dissipator built from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16b00368-b832-202d-3e4f-9b3239c77377"],
 " reproduces the double-commutator generator to machine precision, once a \
single Hamiltonian piece ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"i", "\[Gamma]"}], "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"2", "\[HBar]"}]], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], "}"}], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06d00634-a672-f252-2eef-9871d304c0b8"],
 " is included. That piece is not dissipation: it is a \
frequency-renormalization term, the Lamb shift that the paper's effective \
Hamiltonian absorbs, and it does not touch the positivity verdict. The \
Kossakowski matrix is faithful to the generator. And because the generator is \
now certified to be in GKSL form with a Hermitian, positive-definite ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05feeeaf-4f58-f7b7-3385-07096ad2dd9d"],
 ", the other half of complete positivity comes for free: the map preserves \
the trace and the Hermiticity of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "583a98af-415b-100e-09d9-110970ee6354"],
 " exactly, and Part V watches the completely-positive half play out as a \
covariance that never pierces its floor. Whether that positivity survives \
once more terms of the kernel are kept is the question Part VII takes up, and \
the answer is that it does not: keeping exactly two terms is special."
}], "Text",
 CellID->210724908,ExpressionUUID->"07beae85-a317-6bf9-2d45-47eed6a239c3"],

Cell["\<\
Part V: The Physics Made Visible: Covariance Dynamics and the Uncertainty \
Floor\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1992790374,ExpressionUUID->"503c05d1-55e8-8c5e-01c3-9c9b6382d6a4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A determinant tells us the generator is completely positive; the physics of \
what that buys is clearest for a harmonic potential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60049622-f570-0e0e-103b-0f8ffc055554"],
 ", because there the master equation closes. The Liouvillian is quadratic in \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40ea559d-da93-7842-70ea-4cc6df264aa8"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23ccc6ee-92c0-e596-51f3-dfc8277acffc"],
 ", so the first moments and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "114d8d02-b276-9c05-4772-256fc700e76f"],
 " covariance matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2dc22b63-32d1-862f-5bf1-c34d4765ed75"],
 " form a closed linear system, a drift-plus-diffusion flow"
}], "Text",
 CellID->292747604,ExpressionUUID->"36ea7e2c-072a-2221-5eea-7076b2df710b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "."], "=", 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[UpTee]"], "+", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1553818268,ExpressionUUID->"5b23761c-2477-64e8-0ad1-68464d024e32"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with a drift matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73216bcf-7cf1-61ac-22de-82a9748433f6"],
 " built from the free evolution and the friction, and a diffusion matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69fa63e8-c0ca-4913-1f9a-7ab5f17f1879"],
 " built from the Dekker coefficients. Let us assemble both, verify them, and \
then watch positivity live or die."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1870754514,ExpressionUUID->"409bca18-cbd6-e54d-70b8-ec45ee60cf97"],

Cell["\<\
The first moments obey the classical damped oscillator. Write the drift \
matrix and read its eigenvalues:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1358728755,ExpressionUUID->"10b62b5f-1d3f-f012-404d-c31994cbc378"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Amat", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "M"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "M"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Omega]0", "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "\[Gamma]"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Eigenvalues", "[", "Amat", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"M", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Omega]0", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[25]:= ",
 CellID->935019337,ExpressionUUID->"79984792-c453-565a-2fb8-5edfede63ca0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the eigenvalues are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[PlusMinus]", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d45428e-8fa1-6801-4b7b-5be82a543b6b"],
 ", the two roots of a damped harmonic oscillator with damping rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "604bb87d-3174-a116-1048-32274006f07c"],
 " and frequency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "763191a2-6f8b-197a-1fce-080c0a3e6840"],
 ". Both have negative real part, so the mean position and momentum spiral to \
rest: the first moments know nothing about temperature or ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "635fdfdb-2856-deda-1164-d68549e0a420"],
 ", only about friction."
}], "Text",
 CellID->642744358,ExpressionUUID->"0f6eb37a-d9e9-6713-3515-2b27df9c4a79"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The diffusion lives entirely in the second moments. For this work the \
diffusion matrix is diagonal, carrying position diffusion from the new ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8469dd-bfc7-2a7a-04bb-80873a727940"],
 " and momentum diffusion from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "182ee0c1-720e-fc83-49d5-f9ab07b8c6e9"],
 ". Write it:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1478372881,ExpressionUUID->"3921e4bb-f5e4-3596-68de-fde483969ffc"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Dmat", "[", 
    RowBox[{"dxx_", ",", " ", "dpp_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"2", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"dxx", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "dpp"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Dmat", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"6", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Gamma]", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", 
     RowBox[{"T", "/", 
      RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}]}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "MatrixForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[26]:= ",
 CellID->124263719,ExpressionUUID->"13db9173-5387-1c16-41f8-093d6632677c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The lower entry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6804c0ab-fd16-b7db-183b-d9f4f4a01d21"],
 " is the familiar thermal momentum diffusion that heats the particle; the \
upper entry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"3", 
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77076ae4-09e5-8344-1d3c-83ceaf91d1ae"],
 " is the new position diffusion, small and proportional to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4289b0c6-8043-1b93-72b6-29a031f669f9"],
 ", and identically zero in the standard treatment. These two matrices, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "070f3e08-556d-9d60-2d34-b0525c19e44a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d593b15-c37a-9c59-1b66-b35ef60ce6a3"],
 ", are the whole harmonic dynamics, so they had better be right."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1310926461,ExpressionUUID->"4140e475-1e41-1f16-777f-fe3f9bf4627c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67f13035-938c-831a-0d8e-aa7f263eee60"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16b44e14-0404-e868-3e4c-605eadb6bab2"],
 " against the generator itself, by building the Liouvillian from primitives \
on a truncated oscillator and reading the moment derivatives straight off a \
random state. If the drift and diffusion are correct, the residuals vanish:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1124211690,ExpressionUUID->"70bc3c38-1a7f-2cd8-2043-b6629f0a7622"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", "60"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"hbar", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"mm", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"w0", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "10"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"kt", " ", "=", " ", "5"}], ",", " ", "xop", ",", " ", "pop", ",",
      " ", "hs", ",", "\n", "   ", "ldot", ",", " ", "rho", ",", " ", "blk", ",",
      " ", "sym", ",", " ", "mean", ",", " ", "cov", ",", " ", "lr", ",", " ",
      "dxdt", ",", " ", "dpdt", ",", " ", "dcov", ",", " ", "ap", ",", " ", 
     "dp", ",", " ", "sxp0", ",", " ", "sxpdot"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"xop", ",", " ", "pop"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"oscillatorOps", "[", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "hbar", ",", " ", "mm", ",", " ", "w0"}], 
      "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"hs", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"pop", " ", ".", " ", "pop"}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "mm"}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "mm", " ", 
       RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"xop", " ", ".", " ", "xop"}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ldot", "[", "r_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"I", "/", "hbar"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"hs", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"I", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"gam", "/", "hbar"}], ")"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"xop", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"acomm", "[", 
          RowBox[{"pop", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", "     ", "-",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "gam", " ", "mm", " ", 
         RowBox[{"kt", "/", 
          RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}]}]}], ")"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"xop", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
          RowBox[{"xop", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"gam", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"6", " ", "mm", " ", "kt"}], ")"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"pop", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
          RowBox[{"pop", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "42", "]"}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"blk", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"RandomComplex", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "1"}], " ", "-", " ", "I"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", "I"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"15", ",", " ", "15"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"blk", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"blk", " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "blk", "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"SparseArray", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      "0."}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"rho", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "15"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "15"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
     "blk"}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"rho", "/", 
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "rho", "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"sym", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"xop", " ", ".", " ", "pop"}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"pop", " ", ".", " ", "xop"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], ";", 
    "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"mean", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{"xop", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{"pop", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], ";", "\n",
     "  ", 
    RowBox[{"sxp0", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
       RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
        RowBox[{"sym", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"cov", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
           RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
            RowBox[{"xop", " ", ".", " ", "xop", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], 
            "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"mean", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", "sxp0"}], 
        "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"sxp0", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
           RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
            RowBox[{"pop", " ", ".", " ", "pop", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], 
            "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"mean", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
    ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"lr", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ldot", "[", "rho", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"dxdt", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"xop", " ", ".", " ", "lr"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"dpdt", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"pop", " ", ".", " ", "lr"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"sxpdot", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
       RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
        RowBox[{"sym", " ", ".", " ", "lr"}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"dxdt", " ", 
       RowBox[{"mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "dpdt"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"dcov", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
           RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
            RowBox[{"xop", " ", ".", " ", "xop", " ", ".", " ", "lr"}], 
            "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", 
           RowBox[{"mean", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "dxdt"}]}], ",", " ", 
         "sxpdot"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"sxpdot", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
           RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
            RowBox[{"pop", " ", ".", " ", "pop", " ", ".", " ", "lr"}], 
            "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", 
           RowBox[{"mean", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "dpdt"}]}]}], "}"}]}], 
      "}"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"ap", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Amat", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"M", " ", "->", " ", "mm"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Omega]0", " ", "->", " ", "w0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", " ", "->", " ", "gam"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{"dp", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", 
      RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"gam", "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"6", " ", "mm", " ", "kt"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", "0"}], 
         "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "gam", " ", "mm", " ", 
           RowBox[{"kt", "/", 
            RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"dcov", " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ap", " ", ".", " ", "cov"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"cov", " ", ".", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "ap", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", "dp"}], 
        ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"10.", "^", 
       RowBox[{"-", "6"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[27]:= ",
 CellID->1335749844,ExpressionUUID->"7e10bd94-ae42-3b4d-262f-34d1cbf48997"],

Cell["\<\
As one can see, the covariance residual is the zero matrix: the \
hand-assembled drift and diffusion reproduce the exact generator, computed by \
an entirely independent route on truncated matrices. The Lyapunov flow is \
trustworthy.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->793802945,ExpressionUUID->"5fdf5ac0-01aa-1326-05e5-53aab05f7e0c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now solve for the steady state. Setting ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "."], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "013c2307-fb8b-27c7-30c3-bb60fe3f8d2d"],
 " gives a linear system for the three independent entries of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b734859-75e7-efa6-7901-62030393b58c"],
 "; solve it symbolically with real positive parameters:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->631769182,ExpressionUUID->"4ae31c17-eefa-a706-7a90-96508a8c0a6c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "steady", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"steady", "[", "dmat_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "sxx", ",", " ", "sxp", ",", " ", "spp", ",", " ", "sig", ",", " ", 
       "sol"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"sig", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"sxx", ",", " ", "sxp"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"sxp", ",", " ", "spp"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";", "\n", 
      "   ", 
      RowBox[{"sol", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"First", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Amat", " ", ".", " ", "sig"}], " ", "+", " ", 
              RowBox[{"sig", " ", ".", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "Amat", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
              "dmat"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"sxx", ",", " ", "sxp", ",", " ", "spp"}], "}"}]}], 
         "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"sig", " ", "/.", " ", "sol"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"M", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Omega]0", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"kB", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"T", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sigTW", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"steady", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Dmat", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"6", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Gamma]", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", 
       RowBox[{"T", "/", 
        RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}]}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"sigTW", " ", "//", " ", "MatrixForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[28]:= ",
 CellID->1873681340,ExpressionUUID->"00844d77-2817-3ec6-30bc-653149a3842c"],

Cell["\<\
Read off the steady momentum variance and the steady correlation, the two \
entries where the quantum correction shows:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1468251080,ExpressionUUID->"20b97f64-b973-0c8a-5047-774e380656d0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<\[Sigma]PP\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"sigTW", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<\[Sigma]XP\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"sigTW", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "|>"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[29]:= ",
 CellID->1989234463,ExpressionUUID->"04469009-6b02-dcc3-2c7d-0a530eb4a629"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the steady momentum variance is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"12", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4e35d333-5bd5-ef26-77ca-cb7d5e61b20c"],
 ", the classical equipartition value ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5547dfb6-0e84-e145-037c-d6f0ab36b3af"],
 " plus a small correction of order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12b61bfc-9cd7-eca9-424d-92a61563b6f3"],
 ", and the position-momentum correlation is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"6", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "451364b5-819d-fb99-7321-7dff3029c9e3"],
 ", a purely quantum cross-correlation that is exactly zero in the standard \
treatment. The new position diffusion leaves its fingerprint on the steady \
state, not just on positivity."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1607696641,ExpressionUUID->"13b49e24-0fb7-4441-414b-178eaa422eab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Confirm that this steady state reduces to the classical thermal state when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "445bf28f-7a5a-ecd1-6c78-ebe97fecb63b"],
 ", which is the sanity check every high-temperature master equation must \
pass:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1817342824,ExpressionUUID->"089aa42d-ce49-3603-38b9-3e76ebfd9d69"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
   RowBox[{"sigTW", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "MatrixForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[30]:= ",
 CellID->530774412,ExpressionUUID->"48fccab3-b886-a0f7-7883-e3fd3930f2dd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the classical limit is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"], "/", 
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0cdaad60-2181-5e26-34f9-454a5034250c"],
 ", the Boltzmann covariance of a classical oscillator in thermal \
equilibrium: position variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "542cff75-84e0-b601-7dd3-f73f2c9a1d6b"],
 " and momentum variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00dd9d4d-f7ec-565f-30e2-151681993ca5"],
 ", with no correlation. The quantum corrections are the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d66b502-775d-ec4c-3b1d-2d6c02e9b696"],
 " terms that this limit discards."
}], "Text",
 CellID->599957810,ExpressionUUID->"3a3bfee8-9a0e-4a4b-6bd8-f7b21fbb1891"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Physical states must respect the Robertson-Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger \
uncertainty relation, which for a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "333832e2-8bec-4128-62c7-abcc2d991072"],
 " covariance is the single inequality ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[GreaterEqual]", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78cf51d6-d7cd-4672-28f5-4893e2782d58"],
 ". Check the margin by which the steady state clears this floor:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1899946997,ExpressionUUID->"1d9e3d6f-99f1-7c1e-4ba5-b5491f844764"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Det", "[", "sigTW", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}], "/", "4"}]}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "FullSimplify"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[31]:= ",
 CellID->1051619128,ExpressionUUID->"710db4a8-d877-0db2-2732-2df5d9025798"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the steady margin is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71e12f72-3ad4-a92f-279e-c73cbf66f875"],
 " plus corrections, dominated by a large positive term at high temperature, \
so the steady state sits comfortably above the floor. The standard \
Caldeira-Leggett steady state clears it too. The failure of positivity is \
therefore not a steady-state effect; it is transient, and to see it we must \
watch a specific initial state evolve."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1921351195,ExpressionUUID->"06ea8612-dd18-b4f0-2ee9-185fd4921eda"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here is where the missing term earns its place. Consider a \
minimum-uncertainty initial state that is squeezed in position, narrow in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b02f270-2101-5c3d-3931-f43a50b42707"],
 " and correspondingly broad in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d1868bf-f524-2aaf-5b27-81f8fcd178f5"],
 ", sitting exactly on the floor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "669caa83-24d6-d7e9-0ea3-43ed4d60bd33"],
 ". On the floor with zero correlation, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["det",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"], "\[Prime]"], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], " ", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"], "\[Prime]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ae50fd0-6d1f-8fa4-0a9a-a69a04abd58e"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"], "\[Prime]"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], "11"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66e7a4a8-d710-64fe-0e9c-3df5e2a54ec4"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"], "\[Prime]"], "=", "4", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e73fafe-05d0-7203-6600-f3b8ac654169"],
 ". Compute this rate for standard Caldeira-Leggett, where the position \
diffusion ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], "11"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fb7b09a-ac3b-ef52-254c-29c7c5cfb5b8"],
 " is absent:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1207491739,ExpressionUUID->"12c044c4-b778-74e1-42f0-5da1c20d5ecb"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"ddetFloor", ",", " ", "\[Sigma]XX", ",", " ", "\[Sigma]PP"}], 
   "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ddetFloor", "[", "d11_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"d11", " ", "\[Sigma]PP"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Sigma]XX", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Gamma]", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], " ", "-", " ", "\[Sigma]PP"}], 
         ")"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ddetFloor", "[", "0", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[32]:= ",
 CellID->216741342,ExpressionUUID->"3d9aa029-60a8-273a-6bb9-3a7311428a00"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the standard rate is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64adc082-4122-deff-0c52-d9ec70d4a4c5"],
 ", which is negative precisely when the state is broad in momentum (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]], ">", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e451771-8a55-ceec-267a-8f3b2fe19436"],
 "): the determinant immediately drops below ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4670f053-f537-0b3f-6e0f-ea1cfcc25605"],
 " and the state becomes unphysical. Now compute the term by which this \
work's rate differs, the rescue:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2096934290,ExpressionUUID->"330aabc0-bdd5-22a3-6109-42aa34607089"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ddetFloor", "[", 
    RowBox[{"2", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"6", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "-",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"ddetFloor", "[", "0", "]"}]}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "Simplify"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[33]:= ",
 CellID->1367217003,ExpressionUUID->"38c8cb12-19a5-fbf9-68f7-e35c9851c9c3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, this work adds exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"3", 
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70d705b8-410a-1477-20ec-9ce270bf7f5d"],
 ", proportional to the very momentum variance that caused the trouble, so \
for a strongly squeezed state that term dominates and keeps the rate \
positive. The rescue is not a coincidence of parameters; it is the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "737c509e-bc52-eefb-2104-49d835e4b4c1"],
 " whose sign fixed the Kossakowski determinant, acting now on the covariance."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1372538143,ExpressionUUID->"01a44b6b-c85f-9e0e-375c-6334e9ebe554"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Watch it happen. Solve the covariance flow in closed form from a \
position-squeezed minimum-uncertainty state under both generators, and plot \
how far ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10bcaec6-cc03-bcfd-4043-47a3e5b706c7"],
 " sits above or below the uncertainty floor, zoomed on the early transient \
where the two part ways (the inset carries the full history). The determinant \
is real, so ",
 Cell[BoxData["Re"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25120901-cfbc-a8e6-5321-a16aea4efacc"],
 " only strips the machine-precision residue of the complex-exponential \
solution:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->485911656,ExpressionUUID->"3ee7491f-72c3-8814-669d-61590777db7e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"hbar", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"mm", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"w0", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "10"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"kt", " ", "=", " ", "5"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"eps", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "40"}]}], ",", " ", "a0", ",", " ", "dtw", ",", " ", 
     "dcl", ",", " ", "floor", ",", " ", "run"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"a0", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Amat", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"M", " ", "->", " ", "mm"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Omega]0", " ", "->", " ", "w0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", " ", "->", " ", "gam"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{"dtw", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", 
      RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"gam", "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"6", " ", "mm", " ", "kt"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", "0"}], 
         "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "gam", " ", "mm", " ", 
           RowBox[{"kt", "/", 
            RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{"dcl", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ReplacePart", "[", 
      RowBox[{"dtw", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], 
      "]"}]}], ";", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Caldeira", "-", "Leggett"}], " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"this", " ", "work", " ", "with", " ", "D_XX"}], " ", "->", 
       " ", "0"}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"floor", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}], "/", "4"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"run", "[", "dm_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
        "sxx", ",", " ", "sxp", ",", " ", "spp", ",", " ", "s", ",", " ", "d",
          ",", " ", "sol", ",", " ", "tt"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"s", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"sxx", "[", "tt", "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"sxp", "[", "tt", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"sxp", "[", "tt", "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"spp", "[", "tt", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";", " ", 
        RowBox[{"d", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"a0", " ", ".", " ", "s"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"s", " ", ".", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "a0", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", "dm"}]}], ";",
         "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"sol", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"DSolveValue", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"sxx", "'"}], "[", "tt", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
              RowBox[{"d", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", 
                RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"sxp", "'"}], "[", "tt", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
              RowBox[{"d", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", 
                RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"spp", "'"}], "[", "tt", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
              RowBox[{"d", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", 
                RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
             "       ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"sxx", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
              RowBox[{"eps", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"sxp", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"spp", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
              RowBox[{"1", "/", 
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{"2", " ", "eps"}], ")"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"sxx", ",", " ", "sxp", ",", " ", "spp"}], "}"}], ",", 
           " ", "tt"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
         RowBox[{"u", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"sol", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "[", "u", "]"}], " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"sol", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], "[", "u", "]"}]}], " ", "-", 
             " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"sol", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], "[", "u", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}],
             "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "floor"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n",
     "  ", 
    RowBox[{"With", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"fcl", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"run", "[", "dcl", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ftw", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"run", "[", "dtw", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"fcl", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ftw", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0.15"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0.15"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"-", "0.0032"}], ",", " ", "0.006"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",",
         "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"Red", ",", " ", "Thick"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"Blue", ",", " ", "Thick"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          
          RowBox[{"\"\<t\>\"", ",", 
           " ", "\"\<det \[Sigma](t) - \[HBar]^2/4\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n",
         "    ", 
        RowBox[{
        "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
         " ", "\"\<Early transient: only Caldeira-Leggett pierces the floor\>\
\""}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Placed", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            
            RowBox[{"\"\<Caldeira-Leggett (D_XX = 0)\>\"", ",", 
             " ", "\"\<This work (D_XX > 0)\>\""}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           "Below"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"Dashed", ",", " ", "Gray", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"0.15", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
           "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{"Inset", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"fcl", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"ftw", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
               
               RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"{", "Red", "}"}], ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"{", "Blue", "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", 
               "         ", 
               RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "180"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Style", "[", 
                 
                 RowBox[{"\"\<full range: both thermalize\>\"", ",", " ", 
                  "8"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "         ", 
               RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"Dashed", ",", " ", "Gray", ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"8", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
                 "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Scaled", "[", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"0.72", ",", " ", "0.34"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
          "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "560"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[34]:= ",
 CellID->181917407,ExpressionUUID->"67860241-8011-89c8-0dbd-a42b31a5db12"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the standard Caldeira-Leggett curve dips below the dashed \
floor almost immediately: the squeezed state is driven into the forbidden \
region ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "<", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1318f44b-7a0d-b86f-4127-ee157fb90ab5"],
 ", where the density operator has a negative eigenvalue and is no longer a \
state. The corrected curve never crosses the floor. Both eventually climb to \
the same thermal steady state, as the inset shows, so the distinction is a \
transient one, present exactly when it matters, at the moment of closest \
approach to the quantum limit. The same single term that lifted the \
Kossakowski determinant from negative to positive is what holds the \
covariance above its quantum limit, and the two facts are the same fact seen \
at the level of the matrix and at the level of the trajectory."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1906087345,ExpressionUUID->"221ecbfd-1ed7-d323-5225-e2a79b63be09"],

Cell["Part VI: The Systematic Expansion of the Kernel", "Section",
 CellID->354048744,ExpressionUUID->"3f067a83-888f-4db3-653e-73ed293a1799"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The paper stops one term past white noise, at the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "287fc527-5526-9e30-5804-dc815cd0e51a"],
 " correction, and names its own open problem in the Conclusions: the higher \
order terms in the expansion of the fluctuation paths. Nothing in Part III \
forced the stop. The regularized functional ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["F", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "2", "\[Pi]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", "\[Pi]", 
   UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[Infinity]",
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sinh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "2"}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2207e002-80f7-0285-523c-fa6c308250ef"],
 " accepts the entire Taylor expansion of the fluctuation-path product, and \
every additional power of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "440467ae-8db5-79b4-6c3c-7e0824404b9e"],
 " meets the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["sinh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "2"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "141585f4-d1c1-5bbd-3c2a-1cb1e0742987"],
 " kernel and picks out one more of its moments. This part carries the \
expansion to all orders in closed form, and the tower it builds turns out to \
be the exact Ohmic kernel of Part I, resummed."
}], "Text",
 CellID->786710823,ExpressionUUID->"3d27d006-86b8-9131-64dc-ca603332e01b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The object being expanded is the fluctuation-path product ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "_"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "_"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], "/", "2"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "_"], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], "/", "2"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e44340b-ef5c-51d5-667b-ae548ae9233f"],
 ", even in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "321034f4-436e-dcec-622f-adbe7618a636"],
 " because sending ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "-", 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1287d3f9-6500-de4e-42bc-caa30cbaa494"],
 " only swaps its two factors. Expand it in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3035d7f6-28ea-dcd5-61ca-ceb0489ca63f"],
 " and collect the coefficient of each ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "087f5f2f-6486-1b59-3805-56890d3369a3"],
 ", the objects ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ddf1aac-cdaa-cd7e-2be4-9309e45c9444"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1859374462,ExpressionUUID->"2b41c4a9-15e8-1804-597e-ddf3a39d6b6e"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Clear", "[", 
   RowBox[{"u", ",", " ", "s", ",", " ", "tb", ",", " ", "\[Tau]B"}], "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ser", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"u", "[", 
        RowBox[{"tb", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\[Tau]B", " ", 
          RowBox[{"s", "/", "2"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"u", "[", 
        RowBox[{"tb", " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\[Tau]B", " ", 
          RowBox[{"s", "/", "2"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Coefficient", "[", 
      RowBox[{"ser", ",", " ", "s", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}]}], "]"}], "/", 
     RowBox[{"\[Tau]B", "^", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], ")"}]}]}], " ", "//", " ", "Simplify"}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[35]:= ",
 CellID->544914423,ExpressionUUID->"13ecd9ee-6506-67bb-4193-d0c80cb34d81"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The zeroth coefficient is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6724c974-bdf1-27a5-0edb-e13e3b858d8f"],
 ", the white-noise piece. The first is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", "4"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"], "-", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"\[Prime]", "2"}]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b52875c-0948-9ae8-5961-1f06a8e2e832"],
 ", the single correction the paper keeps. The next brings in the fourth \
derivative ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"]}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "53412643-5a68-df00-017e-b82d5f02a26a"],
 " and the curvature ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "696f5b1d-d56b-3a26-1f15-5346dc1f890c"],
 ", and the pattern holds at every order: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0eb02373-2484-618c-364f-bb3d4d3133d6"],
 " is a bilinear in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640353f1-ff8e-e9b3-0c31-4abafa38bb99"],
 " and its derivatives of total order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "37161f66-4600-a3a8-5d2d-974073baf1f2"],
 ", namely ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", 
     SuperscriptBox["4", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], 
    RowBox[{
     UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["j", "TI"], "+", 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], "=", "2", 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"]}],
      LimitsPositioning->False], 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["(",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         RowBox[{"-", "1"}], 
         StyleBox[")",
          SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["j", "TI"], "!"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["k", "TI"], "!"}]}]], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        StyleBox["j", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}]]}]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e44757e-c407-f813-567c-6d3bedb3cb79"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1088734259,ExpressionUUID->"07a61755-6475-fbf7-2d5d-8f1f0d01c9dd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Inside the action each coefficient is integrated over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "539b0e4e-9e5a-5525-01b8-a0281bef3c0f"],
 ", and integration by parts collapses the bilinear onto a single canonical \
term ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], " ", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "_"], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cd82739-42e3-b7ed-44e7-bf6376971d37"],
 ". The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0971a20b-7913-467e-3f0e-445578a62d44"],
 " in the coefficient and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09df342d-d743-5809-3fe4-ae76e2f62b53"],
 " from moving ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a0cc1e9-e2ca-26d9-3a33-d8b2977c8c23"],
 " derivatives by parts multiply to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "=", "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21fdaace-430e-f3f9-5782-43a876b8c1c3"],
 ", so every term adds with the same sign and the surviving weight is the \
pure combinatorial number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", 
     SuperscriptBox["4", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], 
    RowBox[{
     UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["j", "TI"], "+", 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], "=", "2", 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"]}],
      LimitsPositioning->False], 
     FractionBox["1", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["j", "TI"], "!"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["k", "TI"], "!"}]}]]}]}], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{"2", 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "!"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b4e2dea-4a49-bf2e-4975-c4b46ffd0274"],
 ", independent of the path. Confirm the path-independence on two different \
even fluctuation paths, taking for each the ratio of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Integral]",
    FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "_"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10b057f0-cb39-4e6e-4040-4ebdeecc14b4"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Integral]",
    FontSize->1.15 Inherited], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "_"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41c6bfc6-0792-5005-77fd-36a0b227236f"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->476175344,ExpressionUUID->"62752e4e-571f-d961-120a-c02862aba84b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"xcoef", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "f_", ",", " ", "t_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", 
      RowBox[{"4", "^", "n"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ")"}], "^", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], " ", "-", " ", "j"}], ")"}]}], "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"j", "!"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], " ", "-", " ", "j"}], ")"}], "!"}]}], 
         ")"}]}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"D", "[", 
        RowBox[{"f", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "j"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"D", "[", 
        RowBox[{"f", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], " ", "-", " ", "j"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}],
       ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ratio", "[", "f_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"xcoef", "[", 
          RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "f", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"-", "Infinity"}], ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
       "/", "\n", "      ", 
       RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"f", " ", 
          RowBox[{"D", "[", 
           RowBox[{"f", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"-", "Infinity"}], ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}]}], 
        "]"}]}], " ", "//", " ", "Simplify"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ratio", " ", "/@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      RowBox[{"t", "^", "2"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sech", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[36]:= ",
 CellID->201272189,ExpressionUUID->"34ee5221-bb14-cc46-5c96-4b8b3ea696ac"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ratio is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"1", "/", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166277e1-e8de-815f-3e12-6eca8968d3a5"],
 " for both paths, so the weight is path-independent as the binomial sum \
promised: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Integral]",
    FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "_"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{"2", 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "!"}]], 
   StyleBox["\[Integral]",
    FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "_"], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], " ", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "_"], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ae7a534-7379-468c-3a9c-3d7e060c2cd6"],
 ". At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34baef30-7963-b757-5c59-077a78171dbd"],
 " this is the factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox["1", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15ce0314-20ee-2b64-43f5-9b5e509b764e"],
 " sitting behind the paper's ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "1", 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "38a9ac88-4644-6c0e-6856-45d273f13754"],
 "; at every higher order it is the reciprocal factorial that keeps the \
assembled series under control."
}], "Text",
 CellID->320292756,ExpressionUUID->"64802aa2-b136-451c-0cbf-c30fc0c32c66"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each order carries a moment of the kernel as its weight, the integral of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67771ff6-ea2e-a98b-0d0c-96b38fd8fbd1"],
 " against ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sinh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "2"}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "233ecb8e-17f3-8d32-52c5-e2e8a187d418"],
 ". Part III already met the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7dd949a9-d8cf-50b3-2be7-60f2d97a2299"],
 " case, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[Infinity]",
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sinh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "2"}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "=", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"6", "\[Pi]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a74bc9f-39f4-5114-7a0b-35d9bf81207e"],
 ", the Basel number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], "/", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "598f41e5-f1df-a461-0fb5-58ce806b0f4b"],
 " in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e0f0df5-2071-c96f-4634-a4bf51059bb5"],
 " variable. Compute the family of moments the expansion needs:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1146801282,ExpressionUUID->"7f6e12d5-e3b9-0bb9-2515-8b9e964c5983"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x", "^", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Csch", "[", "x", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[37]:= ",
 CellID->41202278,ExpressionUUID->"41ecc127-3c02-05fa-7793-d881b5b76fc0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "These are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Zeta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "2", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1190ff72-a9fe-60f8-47af-f73fcf8b32c2"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Zeta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "4", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19c80315-d7de-7125-4ff7-9b5ee26b400f"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Zeta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "6", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fdf78a7-59a9-97d9-15e5-7101585dfd23"],
 " up to rational factors, and in closed form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[Infinity]",
       LimitsPositioning->False], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{"2", 
        StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["sinh",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{"-", "2"}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{"2", 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "!"}], " ", 
    StyleBox["\[Zeta]", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{"2", 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "/", 
     SuperscriptBox["2", 
      RowBox[{"2", 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "1"}]]}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7a87483f-bfa4-2eb6-2abd-62793a51749c"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09b26917-59e6-8729-3f41-81515f90ea73"],
 " the Bernoulli numbers. The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], "/", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "521ad179-838d-ce9b-0239-c923363994e1"],
 " that fixed the paper's single correction is the first member of an \
infinite family indexed by the Bernoulli numbers; in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "136d7364-bcfb-8461-4113-6b4e348fef4b"],
 " variable the same family reads ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[Infinity]",
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sinh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "2"}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "/", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b78534b-7a52-d624-5918-4b157fe4bd0e"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1124146653,ExpressionUUID->"30c454b2-bdb8-e427-60fc-4dfc3432cf0d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Multiply each coefficient ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6879dfe8-0276-0c7b-1806-d6b2b7035741"],
 " by its moment and read the result back into the kernel. A term ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Integral]",
    FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "_"], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7cc522fa-6a93-e579-24fa-bba40f27cc43"],
 " in the action is a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b82e386-6ff5-c0ee-09b1-fae009819234"],
 " in the kernel, so the systematic expansion is an even-derivative series ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\[TildeTilde]", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34a39a2f-b372-ffce-5c50-1388c604c514"],
 ". Assemble its coefficients:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1232284935,ExpressionUUID->"66ca9132-7812-8248-0ec9-097c79a4d092"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Clear", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\[Eta]", ",", " ", "\[Tau]B"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"c", "[", "n_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ")"}], "^", "n"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"BernoulliB", "[", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], "]"}], "/", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], ")"}], "!"}]}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Tau]B", "^", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"c", "[", "n", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[38]:= ",
 CellID->2082395230,ExpressionUUID->"023b1c4a-5b09-a8c9-33d8-96145ebdfa13"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first two are exactly the white-noise and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29a4f364-fd74-7ca4-5f5b-eb41f401468e"],
 " coefficients of Part III. The third, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "4"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], "3"], "/", "180"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47740231-7fc8-4299-6d0b-a47b7a7d10e3"],
 ", is the leading new term the paper leaves open, a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1af52337-5e42-c8c3-4a8a-bb715bf49a29"],
 " in the kernel, and its sign is negative. The general coefficient ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"4", 
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{"2", 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]]}], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{"2", 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "!"}]], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "1"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2fdb82dc-2353-e9b3-55f8-1b8656e7bb99"],
 " alternates in sign with the Bernoulli numbers, a fact that will decide \
positivity in the next part. Written out, the kernel three terms past white \
noise is"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2045146513,ExpressionUUID->"5782d92f-a790-094a-7db1-d088d2255b90"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\[TildeTilde]", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"4", 
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]]], 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["B", "TI"]]}], "3"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["B", "TI"], "3"]}], "180"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", "\[Ellipsis]"}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->25123057,ExpressionUUID->"05d48452-325d-a277-33eb-1e1c47e9f15d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The tower is not an arbitrary list of corrections. In Fourier space a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "087ffcf6-194e-431e-3804-f5b098fb2e64"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"i", "\[Omega]"}], "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "615fadf7-df9a-5675-1764-44b0da2f3d5f"],
 ", so the kernel's symbol is a power series in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5de452e3-5fd7-a751-0b9c-4bcd5a630dbb"],
 " whose coefficients are the Bernoulli numbers, the signature of a single \
hyperbolic function. Sum the tower and compare it to the exact Ohmic thermal \
weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["coth",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "/", "2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d0df906-1ebb-1081-5b32-f1609b4e62eb"],
 " of Part I:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->371825621,ExpressionUUID->"519a4e0d-3467-bfb9-07ba-6057bd130583"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Clear", "[", "\[Omega]", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Series", "[", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"c", "[", "n", "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"I", " ", "\[Omega]"}], ")"}], "^", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], ")"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "-",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "\[Omega]", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Coth", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Tau]B", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\[Omega]", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "11"}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[39]:= ",
 CellID->1439628390,ExpressionUUID->"3a891815-8c00-cf41-6ab6-925f25ba95ab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The difference vanishes to every order checked, so the delta-derivative \
tower is the term-by-term Fourier expansion of the exact kernel. The whole \
systematic expansion resums to the colored-noise spectrum we began with in \
Part I, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "=", "\[HBar]", "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0dbacffa-31b0-43f6-3b59-e6a4404511dc"],
 ", and the Bernoulli numbers are its Taylor coefficients. White noise is the \
zeroth term of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}], "2"], 
   StyleBox["coth",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "196a859c-b643-c1b3-4f69-1cd9c3f79399"],
 ", the paper's ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48c8a383-1e42-ef31-78f7-3aed9bf4b21b"],
 " is the first, and keeping all of them is the same as not expanding the \
kernel at all."
}], "Text",
 CellID->497245720,ExpressionUUID->"50735439-04fd-dee7-0001-4e63ac89a4cd"],

Cell["\<\
Part VII: Higher Orders in the Generator, Positivity, and Temperature Reach\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1090726268,ExpressionUUID->"3597ba8d-914b-928f-63ac-33d720ffe0d5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The kernel expansion of Part VI is clean and closed. Turning it into a \
master equation is where the physics turns, because each ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "056fda38-a5bc-2884-3314-dc65cc497aee"],
 " must be handed to an operator, and only the first two land in the tidy \
two-operator Lindblad form. This part maps the higher terms, asks whether the \
extended generator is still completely positive, and measures how far down in \
temperature each new term reaches."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2124519200,ExpressionUUID->"383c4a9f-130c-f8c1-69c4-63d9a6beca2b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The map of Part IV sent ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b649e79-a2e1-7610-291b-1022d6945d7a"],
 " to the position operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09cb884c-5fc8-b209-3fc8-22165a620153"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "376c6589-bcca-29e8-5d14-7cd3357f7b32"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], "/", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "667bb688-7420-22c7-0e18-2fd27dd5702d"],
 ", the velocity, because a white noise multiplying ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]}],
    AutoSpacing->False], "."]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72002252-da4c-5210-223f-c41fdff9217a"],
 " couples to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], "."], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], "/", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "084561a7-5440-aaee-387b-78015dfaf834"],
 ". The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "721e71e5-9ca7-ded5-2226-68cf1553a43f"],
 " term multiplies ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]}],
    AutoSpacing->False], ".."]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a84e7eb-55e0-1894-3abb-feb563956afe"],
 ", so its operator is the acceleration ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], ".."]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3261920b-7b77-02d6-621e-14557e02503c"],
 " under the system Hamiltonian, fixed by the Heisenberg relation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], ".."], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["S", "TI"]], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["S", "TI"]], ",", 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebe3b2c-9c8f-bd2d-7645-b376153b0477"],
 ". Evaluate that double commutator on a truncated oscillator, for a harmonic \
and a quartic potential, and compare it to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d6a0058-fb4a-caff-2b69-9a05fefc98c5"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->617350884,ExpressionUUID->"41d92934-9aba-8299-77e6-c17e1f4cd0e3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", "40"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"hbar", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"mm", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"w0", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"lam", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "7"}]}], ",", " ", "xop", ",", " ", "pop", ",", " ", 
     "hHarm", ",", " ", "hQuart", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"top", " ", "=", " ", "25"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"xop", ",", " ", "pop"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"oscillatorOps", "[", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "hbar", ",", " ", "mm", ",", " ", "w0"}], 
      "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"hHarm", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"pop", " ", ".", " ", "pop"}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "mm"}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "mm", " ", 
       RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"xop", " ", ".", " ", "xop"}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"hQuart", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"pop", " ", ".", " ", "pop"}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "mm"}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"lam", " ", 
       RowBox[{"MatrixPower", "[", 
        RowBox[{"xop", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
       RowBox[{"Abs", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Flatten", "@", 
         RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{"I", "/", "hbar"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
              RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
               RowBox[{"hHarm", ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"hHarm", ",", " ", "xop"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", "+",
              " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}], " ", "xop"}]}], ")"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "top"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "top"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], 
          "]"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
       RowBox[{"Abs", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Flatten", "@", 
         RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{"I", "/", "hbar"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
              RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
               RowBox[{"hQuart", ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"hQuart", ",", " ", "xop"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
             "       ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"4", " ", "lam", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"MatrixPower", "[", 
                RowBox[{"xop", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "/", "mm"}]}]}], ")"}],
            "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "top"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "top"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], 
          "]"}]}]}]}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[40]:= ",
 CellID->1357963930,ExpressionUUID->"5cc23ff5-bf0f-f019-04f1-b6bf3abbc363"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both residuals vanish, confirming ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], ".."], "=", "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29880975-91f0-008f-5fb7-a13f278552d5"],
 ", the force divided by the mass. The first time derivative ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], "."], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], "/", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "551c00cf-fc58-99c4-0323-99a8f5d2eb2e"],
 " was kinematic, the same for every potential, which is why ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "22235db8-54be-42b7-53d1-54e25d4b109d"],
 " produced a universal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0976d5ae-737d-f257-3f0d-cc080609c0bd"],
 " term. The second is not: it is the force, so the operator carried by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13e711b4-4d78-4d68-419c-88fe640d17b2"],
 " depends on the potential. For a free particle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3fd09d86-aea1-a602-65ef-14e3cb550d68"],
 " and it vanishes, so the series truncates at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f6c0922-6605-ed68-5513-a08c13b1b7b2"],
 " and the two-operator generator is exact to all orders. For the harmonic \
potential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], "=", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2caab86a-2af9-b1b1-54a9-32344e8d039b"],
 " it is proportional to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f56169e-4783-4dbb-256d-8fd872361781"],
 " again, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b84d4d6-858d-5842-09bb-cd902c382aa8"],
 " folds back into the position channel and only renormalizes its \
coefficient. For an anharmonic potential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], "\[Proportional]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], "3"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67558936-e5eb-8680-0d6a-2173939fecea"],
 " and beyond, it is a genuinely new Lindblad operator and the generator \
leaves the two-operator family. This is what the paper meant by higher orders \
being future work: past ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1072dc7c-f7d5-c74e-4001-d6398261ad94"],
 ", the generator's operator content is potential-dependent."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1626918454,ExpressionUUID->"3462f0a3-098c-f6b3-5c11-e90da83edc99"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The natural guess for a higher momentum-diffusion term is a quartic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], "2"], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], "2"], ",", 
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04cac1af-436c-9192-2cc9-d809761ee3f8"],
 ", from reading each time derivative as one power of momentum. The \
computation says otherwise: two derivatives make an acceleration, not a \
squared momentum, so the operator is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63be94f2-239e-9b81-1145-0dbc5628e9eb"],
 ", not ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5a3d7a71-218e-1995-0bc3-7c3b503b6bff"],
 ". A second surprise waits in the sign. Each channel carries a noise \
variance, related to the kernel coefficient by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Kappa]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "=", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "=", "4", 
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "1"}]], "/", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a0f2024-2f71-09ca-6a34-b98e4a045b10"],
 ": the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "277956ac-4c9d-d338-4d07-4ff66529be02"],
 " paired time derivatives put back the alternating sign that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "178a6a52-23e4-1142-3d89-8c1c559163a8"],
 " carried, so the variance is left with the bare sign of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52ddf811-e480-8137-02e2-f25a8d3ad01d"],
 ", and complete positivity needs each ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Kappa]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "719ae17a-c654-ed44-27b9-f927f3e6b7ae"],
 " non-negative. Read those signs off the Bernoulli numbers:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->675379980,ExpressionUUID->"62c8f42b-c628-388a-12f7-ee74f3c28ad0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Sign", "[", 
    RowBox[{"BernoulliB", "[", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[41]:= ",
 CellID->1331866192,ExpressionUUID->"36e5ffeb-8179-694d-5e9a-f6b5300c3b97"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first two are positive, which is precisely why the two-term generator \
of Part IV is completely positive: the white-noise channel and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7af061c8-c44a-ae8e-2a80-7895edfcf4d4"],
 " momentum channel are both legitimate. But ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], "4"], "<", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d437dad-8290-de9a-3b71-74f7372aa4e0"],
 ", so the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7aafc905-908a-67da-2a54-e16f213f4d20"],
 " channel has a negative variance, an anti-diffusion. Complete positivity is \
therefore not a property the series carries term by term; it is a coincidence \
of the first two Bernoulli signs. Only the full resummation is safe, because \
the exact spectrum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["coth",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "/", "2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62016b94-8ad8-fb56-123e-82de2f52c9bc"],
 " is non-negative at every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0e7c794a-82c2-56e7-3604-711437773ccd"],
 ", so the exact non-Markovian influence functional is a genuine positive \
Gaussian even where its local truncations are not."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1391655620,ExpressionUUID->"30f601cf-5001-fb68-608d-98a961b5c9b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "See the obstruction directly. A negative-variance channel is a double \
commutator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04bc0f0b-f02f-243d-2c43-a75481db8f07"],
 " entering with a positive coefficient, the wrong (anti-diffusion) sign for \
decoherence, and for the anharmonic case ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], "\[Proportional]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], "3"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a24bdc2-598a-1b95-4bdb-34ac583f69ff"],
 ". For a pure state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "705e212e-f5a4-7717-2065-b88bfc515a7d"],
 " and any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "\[Perpendicular]", 
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c2f5325-a3f6-c048-05d5-4a8ed5809292"],
 ", the quadratic form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]},
      "Bra"], 
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["[",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
       StyleBox["]",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", "2"}], 
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {
        RowBox[{
         TemplateBox[{
           StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]},
          "Bra"], 
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
         TemplateBox[{
           StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
          "Ket"]}]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "211ecaf2-61ee-418f-5725-e3bc179b13d5"],
 " is negative, so one anti-diffusion step must push an eigenvalue of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51e4dffc-d38f-5703-079b-d6b9e63a3a69"],
 " below zero. Apply it to the oscillator ground state and read the smallest \
eigenvalue:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->861714746,ExpressionUUID->"30e43b5d-74af-d0fb-609b-b3077d5ba2c1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", "40"}], ",", " ", "xop", ",", " ", "pop", ",",
      " ", "aop", ",", " ", "psi", ",", " ", "rho"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"xop", ",", " ", "pop"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"oscillatorOps", "[", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], ";",
     "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"aop", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"MatrixPower", "[", 
      RowBox[{"xop", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"psi", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
      RowBox[{"SparseArray", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "n", "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", "psi", ",", " ", "psi"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n",
     "  ", 
    RowBox[{"Min", "@", 
     RowBox[{"Eigenvalues", "[", 
      RowBox[{"rho", " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "100"}], ")"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
         RowBox[{"aop", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
           RowBox[{"aop", ",", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[42]:= ",
 CellID->1192942815,ExpressionUUID->"44d9380c-2e05-8f35-6ce6-b2564bb1d21f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The smallest eigenvalue is exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "3", "/", "80"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36758762-649a-f7b1-5e0a-1f4c0d2cdd9b"],
 ", negative: after a single step under the anti-diffusion, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "138e1639-4d05-8b97-41b5-886364b1d9fd"],
 " has left the set of states. This is the honest verdict on the extended \
generator. Truncated at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "156728ce-0023-e03b-431c-c1a8b1d7b301"],
 " for an anharmonic potential it is not completely positive, because the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], "4"], "<", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fc37353-2ed8-42c8-25f1-6b1d4b6d1012"],
 " channel is anti-diffusive and its operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], "3"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26ff5c08-e081-ff27-4e85-56559135c20d"],
 " cannot be absorbed into the position and momentum channels. The paper's \
guaranteed Lindblad form is genuinely special to the two-term order, not the \
first step of a term-by-term positive series."
}], "Text",
 CellID->556077107,ExpressionUUID->"07c988c4-3ef2-8066-2df6-21aeba84d34c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The higher terms are not useless, though. For the harmonic potential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4bc0a2f3-6150-447f-79ff-3bbd10e52f45"],
 " folds into the position channel, and there it sharpens the equilibrium. On \
the stationary paths ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["X", "TI"]}],
     AutoSpacing->False], ".."], "=", "-", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ac66077-3bfa-1f18-2afe-7a31bd8f6262"],
 ", so the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d863d84-94ab-5643-6bbd-b4ee1d5e3ca9"],
 " term adds an effective white-noise weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "4"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "4"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ab8b877-e011-189c-2a47-323091a46ae6"],
 " to the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35eb0178-2238-e094-63e8-992257b2b2fe"],
 " channel and shifts the momentum-diffusion coefficient by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "4"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "4"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", "\[HBar]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0da6433d-a7a4-ba24-3b5e-5b66d256090e"],
 ", through the same weight-over-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[HBar]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "462f64f6-435d-c7dd-6fd5-7db076e9ad27"],
 " map as Part IV. Recompute the steady momentum variance with this shift and \
compare, order by order in ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b06bf63-5f43-ed7c-793d-374d5af7b446"],
 ", to the exact quantum Gibbs value ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"]}], "2"], 
   StyleBox["coth",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"]}], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0fd1c247-21a4-d962-35ee-e4215056a848"],
 ". First the two-term generator:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->15883883,ExpressionUUID->"09347675-9fce-c17b-38cc-683f1a789041"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sPPgibbs", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", "M", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Omega]0", "/", "2"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Coth", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Omega]0", "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"DXX", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"6", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"DPP", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Gamma]", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", 
    RowBox[{"T", "/", 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"steady", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Dmat", "[", 
        RowBox[{"DXX", ",", " ", "DPP"}], "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
     "sPPgibbs"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[43]:= ",
 CellID->308842859,ExpressionUUID->"2c597ed5-00d9-d535-5467-779fb16dbc1f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two-term generator reproduces the Gibbs momentum variance through order \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c4d8d6-27c8-a0db-0efb-d1905262f221"],
 ", and the first discrepancy is order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "4"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d3801b6-8b23-0df3-74c7-98f02ed657d9"],
 ". Now add the harmonic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09816d05-11e9-fb6e-3fbe-856fa79dc9b4"],
 " shift and recompute:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1108042358,ExpressionUUID->"35ec423d-cde2-7917-6394-6466eb97487d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"dppShift", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "\[Eta]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[Tau]B", "^", "3"}], "/", "180"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Omega]0", "^", "4"}], "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[HBar]"}], ")"}]}]}], " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"M", " ", "\[Gamma]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Tau]B", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"steady", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Dmat", "[", 
        RowBox[{"DXX", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"DPP", " ", "+", " ", "dppShift"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
     "sPPgibbs"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "7"}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[44]:= ",
 CellID->1009200201,ExpressionUUID->"05e0e9bc-56b1-1bf2-339f-00e6634469d8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46408f14-a324-388b-6e7f-2751d6d68ad1"],
 " correction cancels the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "4"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40213c85-9219-7c2b-71de-b5ef27ac4771"],
 " discrepancy exactly, and the agreement with the Gibbs state now holds \
through order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "4"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "678faed4-2cca-f411-0db4-479e457cdf7b"],
 ", the residual pushed down to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "6"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b3cac94-919f-f08d-6ac3-45de202bc2d7"],
 ". Each order of the fluctuation-path expansion buys one more power of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "634a1270-2707-566e-1149-943a52b23cb4"],
 " in the equilibrium match, so the systematic expansion is literally an \
expansion in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"], "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "571f0194-b08e-3ab4-7d24-98d1c138889e"],
 ": the higher terms carry the master equation's validity from high \
temperature down toward the quantum regime, one Bernoulli number at a time."
}], "Text",
 CellID->752465254,ExpressionUUID->"79764466-e076-5945-2f0e-5e4391032baf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That downward reach has a floor. The expansion parameter is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "=", "\[HBar]", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54e8dec7-14b1-519a-7c97-d7a19d4423e0"],
 ", and the series is the Taylor expansion of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["coth",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25f5c72f-3423-741a-538a-de89bdd65f60"],
 ", which converges only up to the nearest singularity of the hyperbolic \
cotangent. Locate it:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->891183881,ExpressionUUID->"6dbbd446-5835-e39a-1b58-ce2059c1b1e0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"z", " ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sinh", "[", 
       RowBox[{"z", "/", "2"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     
     RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Im", "[", "z", "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
      RowBox[{"4", " ", "Pi"}]}]}], ",", " ", "z"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[45]:= ",
 CellID->741634648,ExpressionUUID->"6d34e655-b983-17e8-14cb-f81f38367d32"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The nearest pole sits at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], "=", "2", "\[Pi]", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c435daa-0d1c-c5df-0471-54f4a4aeaf25"],
 ", that is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "=", "2", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21714cd0-c04e-e57a-570f-659df1f8cc40"],
 ", the first bosonic Matsubara frequency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "=", "2", "\[Pi]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74ff421b-073b-c6d4-1c85-6445b2cfac3e"],
 ". The delta-derivative tower converges only for frequencies below it, so \
the whole Markovian construction is a statement about modes with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "\[LessTilde]", "2", "\[Pi]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3ebc3a74-dd7c-3fa6-6643-bc31d40e858c"],
 ". For the harmonic oscillator this is the condition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[GreaterTilde]", "\[HBar]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"], "/", "2", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d5c93fe-a057-3a16-2b63-0abbd1e3897c"],
 ": below it, the first Matsubara mode makes the bath memory genuinely \
non-Markovian and no finite number of delta-derivatives can follow. That ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "487dadd0-5ed6-7873-7802-449a5b634b59"],
 " carries two meanings at once. It is the convergence radius of the harmonic \
observable, whose series inherited the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"1", "/", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5219761b-8a64-c9ff-0227-68452f169bc5"],
 " of the smooth-path reduction of Part VI; and it is the boundary of useful \
truncation for the bare expansion, whose raw moments ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "!"}], " ", 
   StyleBox["\[Zeta]", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "/", 
    SuperscriptBox["2", 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "1"}]]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69346765-6d1c-e9c9-18cc-7f4f04aebb13"],
 " grow factorially on their own, so the underlying series in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["B", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c22b8c2-70f4-0562-25d1-31ac00816c48"],
 " is asymptotic rather than convergent, and the reciprocal factorials of a \
smooth path are exactly what rescue it. This is the precise temperature reach \
the paper's motivation invokes, and the precise place the systematic \
expansion ends."
}], "Text",
 CellID->359589406,ExpressionUUID->"04fec585-b88c-469b-2c85-dcef39392ce1"],

Cell["Part VIII: The Hu-Paz-Zhang Benchmark", "Section",
 CellID->533832725,ExpressionUUID->"7aa617d4-4041-969d-2a5d-8e9e71f5fce7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The generator of Parts IV and V is Markovian: constant coefficients, and a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e86e5c8-d785-1389-06bd-fc95e23061d3"],
 " term. The exact reduced dynamics of the same harmonic particle in a real \
bath is the Hu-Paz-Zhang dynamics, with time-dependent coefficients and no ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3582ea65-851b-2569-63b1-0c4f2caf8fb3"],
 " term at all, so the constant-coefficient generator is not a limit of it in \
any naive sense. The paper argues this is a feature: taking ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "\[Rule]", "\[Infinity]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e81d752-d9a7-cf7a-06be-cf1fd8539240"],
 " in the other master equations of Table I also forces ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "\[Infinity]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6dc17641-57cc-3497-1bff-682b627e9efd"],
 ", collapsing the kernel to a pure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "647a9320-5a37-336f-0c19-0a8a5fc381b5"],
 " and losing positivity, whereas keeping the next kernel term lets ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "\[Rule]", "\[Infinity]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57b40e76-1aa6-da65-7d4b-a0309f50a94f"],
 " at fixed temperature. Whether the constant-coefficient generator is \
nonetheless the correct Markovian limit is a quantitative question, and for a \
harmonic system it is fully answerable, because the reduced dynamics of a \
linear bath is Gaussian and can be computed exactly from the microscopic \
model, with no master equation in between. The Hu-Paz-Zhang master equation \
is only the analytic packaging of that exact dynamics; here we compute the \
dynamics itself and let the constant-coefficient generator stand next to it."
}], "Text",
 CellID->739917449,ExpressionUUID->"575b10e3-003a-b957-7d78-89cdb1cc0bbd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The microscopic model is the Caldeira-Leggett Hamiltonian with the bath \
written out: the harmonic system coupled to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["N", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c7345dd-208f-a284-2401-5c87513bf0ee"],
 " oscillators whose frequencies and couplings discretize the Ohmic spectral \
density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0121a537-2575-8479-30de-3d714c01ef43"],
 ", the counter-term keeping ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f325126-465a-e19d-26c2-488073ecb3e7"],
 " physical. The whole Hamiltonian is quadratic, so the full phase-space \
covariance evolves exactly under the symplectic flow ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"A", "t"}], "TI"]], "\[CapitalSigma]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[UpTee]"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "739af998-c5c1-31b3-21b9-f0c5ec758399"],
 ", and its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "003becda-d908-4451-31d8-0587d8bd2ebb"],
 " system block is the exact reduced covariance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7aeb468a-2cc6-59e2-2ae9-5fd445732bc8"],
 ". Since ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["G", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3873a668-04d7-31ac-6800-3832ad6383f6"],
 " is a symplectic (Hamiltonian) generator, its spectrum is purely imaginary \
and the propagated covariance is real. Build the propagator, with the bath \
sampled thermally and the system in the squeezed state of Part V, and confirm \
the discretization has reached the continuum by comparing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["N", "TI"], "=", "200"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4156c81a-8a68-59d7-776d-e2442f1d2b3d"],
 " against ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["N", "TI"], "=", "300"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e7ab4-00f8-e339-7ea6-73feb172ce03"],
 " modes over the whole window used below. The finite bath recurs at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[TildeTilde]", "2", "\[Pi]", 
   StyleBox["N", "TI"], "/", "\[CapitalOmega]", "\[TildeTilde]", "42"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b3ec616-de69-0141-3ac5-d853db1c53ab"],
 " for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["N", "TI"], "=", "200"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c0d57bf-7ae8-3253-2433-4ef97e8280b9"],
 ", so every window in this part stays before that revival:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->473762610,ExpressionUUID->"0aaecb0d-dff0-cd78-3a55-e356d98a9442"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "exactPieces", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"exactPieces", "[", 
    RowBox[{"nn_", ",", " ", "cutoff_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"mm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"w0", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"eta", " ", "=", " ", "0.1"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"kT", " ", "=", " ", "5."}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"eps", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"1", "/", "40."}]}], ",", " ", "sys0", ",", " ", "dw", ",", 
       " ", "wk", ",", " ", "ck", ",", " ", "dim", ",", " ", "g", ",", " ", 
       "jm", ",", " ", "amat", ",", " ", "sig0", ",", " ", "vals", ",", " ", 
       "vecs", ",", " ", "vv", ",", " ", "vinv", ",", " ", "th"}], "}"}], ",",
      "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"sys0", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"eps", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"1", "/", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"2", " ", "eps"}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";", 
      "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"dw", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"N", "[", 
        RowBox[{"cutoff", "/", "nn"}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"wk", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Range", "[", "nn", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ")"}], " ", "dw"}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ck", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"wk", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"4", " ", "eta", " ", 
          RowBox[{"dw", "/", "Pi"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"dim", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"nn", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"SparseArray", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"mm", " ", 
                RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"ck", "^", "2"}], "/", 
                 RowBox[{"wk", "^", "2"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
              RowBox[{"1", "/", "mm"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "       ", 
           RowBox[{"Flatten", "@", 
            RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"2", " ", "k"}], " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"2", " ", "k"}], " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}], 
                 " ", "->", " ", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"wk", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"[", "k", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"2", " ", "k"}], " ", "+", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"2", " ", "k"}], " ", "+", " ", "2"}]}], "}"}], 
                 " ", "->", " ", "1."}], ",", "\n", "          ", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"2", " ", "k"}], " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}], 
                 " ", "->", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"-", 
                  RowBox[{"ck", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"[", "k", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"2", " ", "k"}], " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
                   "1"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"-", 
                  RowBox[{"ck", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"[", "k", "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "nn"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"dim", ",", " ", "dim"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
      "   ", 
      RowBox[{"jm", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"SparseArray", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Band", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"-", "1."}], ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"nn", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";",
       "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"amat", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
        RowBox[{"jm", " ", ".", " ", "g"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"th", "[", "w_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Coth", "[", 
             RowBox[{"w", "/", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"2", " ", "kT"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], "/", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"2", " ", "w"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"w", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Coth", "[", 
              RowBox[{"w", "/", 
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{"2", " ", "kT"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], "/", "2"}]}]}], 
          "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"sig0", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
        RowBox[{"SparseArray", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Band", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", "sys0", "}"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"th", " ", "/@", " ", "wk"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";", 
      "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"vals", ",", " ", "vecs"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Eigensystem", "[", "amat", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"vv", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "vecs", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"vinv", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Inverse", "[", "vv", "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
         RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
           RowBox[{"With", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"vv", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"[", 
                  RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".", 
                " ", 
                RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"vals", " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", "vinv"}], 
                 ")"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"p", " ", ".", " ", "sig0", " ", ".", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "p", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",",
         "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
         RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
           RowBox[{"With", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"vv", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"[", 
                   RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".",
                  " ", 
                 RowBox[{"(", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"vals", " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", "vinv"}], 
                  ")"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"pd", " ", "=", " ", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"vv", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"[", 
                   RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".",
                  " ", 
                 RowBox[{"(", 
                  RowBox[{"vals", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"vals", " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", "vinv"}], 
                  ")"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"pd", " ", ".", " ", "sig0", " ", ".", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "p", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
              RowBox[{"p", " ", ".", " ", "sig0", " ", ".", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "pd", "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], 
        ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
         RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"vv", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
               RowBox[{"vals", " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", 
              RowBox[{"vinv", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", 
                RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "2"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
             ")"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
         RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"vv", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"vals", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
               RowBox[{"vals", " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", 
              RowBox[{"vinv", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", 
                RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "2"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
             ")"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
         RowBox[{"Abs", "@", 
          RowBox[{"Re", "[", "vals", "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"pieces", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"exactPieces", "[", 
    RowBox[{"200", ",", " ", "30"}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"p300", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"First", "[", 
    RowBox[{"exactPieces", "[", 
     RowBox[{"300", ",", " ", "30"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
     RowBox[{"Abs", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"First", "[", "pieces", "]"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "-", 
        " ", 
        RowBox[{"p300", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "38", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[46]:= ",
 CellID->1751712322,ExpressionUUID->"4fe4a286-576e-fd11-759b-3be06218c47b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["N", "TI"], "=", "200"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07179650-9fbb-2bc1-2d2c-081a1a4e792b"],
 " versus ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["N", "TI"], "=", "300"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7aecd320-e31f-2936-2a93-ca8d96aa781c"],
 " covariance difference is negligible across the whole window, so a few \
hundred modes reproduce the continuum Ohmic bath everywhere the dynamics is \
read below. Confirm too that the full drift is a symplectic generator, its \
spectrum purely imaginary, so the propagated covariance is real and reading \
the real part strips only machine residue:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1390140890,ExpressionUUID->"326b0854-5043-0b63-6268-a21e61f65649"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Last", "[", "pieces", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[47]:= ",
 CellID->1031105928,ExpressionUUID->"1d6edc53-4ce5-e0f2-4b15-d61d6491b2d8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The spectral real part is machine zero, so the construction is a genuine \
oscillatory, energy-conserving flow. This ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "45f7e4e6-4e1c-a184-738c-fdc06baef3ee"],
 " is the exact answer, the target the Markovian generator must hit."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1410588720,ExpressionUUID->"70e98525-204e-6ba4-2096-1c8f51fb398e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Read off the drift and diffusion the exact dynamics carries. Written as a \
covariance flow ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "."], "=", 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "\[UpTee]"], "+", 
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "704169dd-a4db-5005-207e-8086cd6e236f"],
 ", the instantaneous drift is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["G", "TI"], "."], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b2d1c14-5aff-cd5f-2ad2-965e5e8b97a5"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["G", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62ac11c1-6d0b-a8c0-1253-88ab04bffa2a"],
 " the reduced first-moment propagator, and the diffusion is what remains. \
These coefficients ring persistently rather than settle, so read each one's \
time-average (its center) and its range over a window, and set the centers \
beside the Markovian values ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e7621e1-2fba-a33a-560d-b8cb4a4c0e00"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15938457-0322-a4d9-43a0-1e11b6d40e23"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1051974278,ExpressionUUID->"7f1ed2e3-b722-4b37-2525-cbccc2d7161d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"sig", ",", " ", "sigd", ",", " ", "gprop", ",", " ", "gpropd"}], 
    "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"pieces", "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"adAt", "[", "t_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"gpropd", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Inverse", "[", 
          RowBox[{"gprop", "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", "d"}], "}"}],
      ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"d", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"sigd", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"a", " ", ".", " ", 
         RowBox[{"sig", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"sig", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "a", "]"}]}]}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "d"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ts", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
       RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "20.", ",", " ", "0.25"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     "fr", ",", " ", "dxx", ",", " ", "dpp", ",", " ", "dxp", ",", " ", 
     "stat"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"fr", ",", " ", "dxx", ",", " ", "dpp", ",", " ", "dxp"}], 
      "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"With", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"ad", " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{"adAt", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"ad", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
            " ", 
            RowBox[{"ad", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
            " ", 
            RowBox[{"ad", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
            " ", 
            RowBox[{"ad", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
           "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "ts"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"stat", "[", "x_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "x", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Min", "[", "x", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Max", "[", "x", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "1.*^-10"}], 
      "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"Grid", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<center\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<min\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<max\>\""}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"stat", "[", "fr", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<friction\>\""}], 
         "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"stat", "[", "dxx", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<D_XX\>\""}], 
         "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"stat", "[", "dpp", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<D_PP\>\""}], 
         "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"stat", "[", "dxp", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<D_XP\>\""}], 
         "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Alignment", " ", "->", " ", "Left"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[48]:= ",
 CellID->1989924844,ExpressionUUID->"52e63e44-9d5c-26a1-029d-b02e14ee8c8b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Against the constant drift of Part V, whose friction entry is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e766a94-5ec6-6187-160d-83de5b7333ed"],
 ", and its diagonal diffusion ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], "=", "2", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], " ", 
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2eead67c-41e5-1519-56e9-c82677907c63"],
 ", three features stand out. The exact coefficients do not settle to \
constants: they oscillate persistently around centers that are exactly the \
Markovian values, the friction around ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23a655ec-dad2-e192-515e-4cc9df64b3f8"],
 " and the momentum diffusion around the classical Einstein value ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "=", "2", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62ef85cc-c62f-39ac-1294-1ca9f3db8bf6"],
 ". The propagator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d6c313b-6800-4a9b-2b13-a96509b518e1"],
 " rings slowly, at the system frequency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75dfb56b-bb47-a02b-23e4-2d353ef3f371"],
 ", but the extracted coefficient ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["G", "TI"], "."], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57533ce7-69d6-be0e-7d60-b5c108600554"],
 " divides out that decaying envelope and exposes the bath's fast memory \
underneath, so it rings far faster, at the cutoff ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27c3fefb-2ee6-8038-4df0-f7a54a90d302"],
 "; the oscillation does not damp, its Markovian center is reached almost at \
once on the short memory time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Tilde]", "1", "/", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60d4995f-bb7f-b80c-10eb-11193e0b0b56"],
 ", and the ringing is what the constant-coefficient generator smooths away. \
The position-diffusion entry, though, is not merely centered on zero, it is \
identically zero at every time, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64608bbe-760c-8af3-0c1f-22f803bed8d9"],
 ": Hu-Paz-Zhang has no ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09661063-a2cf-675e-3f1d-8a4cd77a4da4"],
 " term. So the dominant momentum diffusion agrees with this work, and the \
difference is in the small correction, where this work carries a constant \
position diffusion ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5561d787-26b0-8d0a-031e-cee1534ad450"],
 " and no cross, while the exact dynamics carries an anomalous cross ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0fea91e8-e80e-a1ed-35e9-08b589b8f337"],
 " centered on zero and no position diffusion: two memoryless stand-ins for \
the same memory, both completely positive."
}], "Text",
 CellID->695529426,ExpressionUUID->"37725419-c8bf-c4cd-5d02-4e42e94bae17"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the physical test, the uncertainty floor of Part V. A position-squeezed \
state starts on the floor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6eee5857-8f9d-bf63-1696-52112a290249"],
 ". Compute the smallest margin ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2635f536-2fc9-ab3c-4fca-ed704a7df606"],
 " reaches over the whole evolution, for the exact dynamics, this work, and \
standard Caldeira-Leggett:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->767788723,ExpressionUUID->"1b3760e9-4a32-92b2-4acd-79b36fc4e098"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"mm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"w0", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "10"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"kT", " ", "=", " ", "5."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"sys0", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"1", "/", "80"}], ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "20."}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", "am", ",",
      " ", "dm", ",", " ", "dcl", ",", " ", "ssm", ",", " ", "ssc", ",", " ", 
     "sm", ",", " ", "sc"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"am", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "mm"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "mm"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "gam"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{"dm", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"gam", "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"6", " ", "mm", " ", "kT"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", "0."}], 
         "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "gam", " ", "mm", " ", "kT"}]}], "}"}]}], 
       "}"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"dcl", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"4", " ", "gam", " ", "mm", " ", "kT"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
    ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"ssm", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"LyapunovSolve", "[", 
      RowBox[{"am", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "dm"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ssc", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"LyapunovSolve", "[", 
      RowBox[{"am", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "dcl"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"sm", "[", "t_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"e", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
          RowBox[{"am", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ssm", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"e", " ", ".", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"sys0", " ", "-", " ", "ssm"}], ")"}], " ", ".", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "e", "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"sc", "[", "t_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"e", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
          RowBox[{"am", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ssc", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"e", " ", ".", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"sys0", " ", "-", " ", "ssc"}], ")"}], " ", ".", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "e", "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"Chop", "@", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Min", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
            RowBox[{"sig", "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "35", ",", " ", "0.05"}], 
           "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
       RowBox[{"Min", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
            RowBox[{"sm", "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "35", ",", " ", "0.05"}], 
           "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
       RowBox[{"Min", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
            RowBox[{"sc", "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "35", ",", " ", "0.05"}], 
           "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[49]:= ",
 CellID->494419947,ExpressionUUID->"14fe93a8-4ee9-5b9e-3c85-0af26a9c29e4"],

Cell["\<\
The exact dynamics and this work never go negative over the entire evolution; \
only Caldeira-Leggett does, dipping below the floor into the region where the \
density operator has a negative eigenvalue. The exact curve cannot cross the \
floor, because the reduced state of a genuine unitary evolution is a state at \
every instant; that this work stays above it too is the covariance-level face \
of its guaranteed positivity. See it, zoomed on the early transient where the \
three part ways, with the full relaxation in the inset:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1581507689,ExpressionUUID->"11cf5d11-52cc-ddbb-47f5-555b677ea781"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"mm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"w0", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "10"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"kT", " ", "=", " ", "5."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"sys0", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"1", "/", "80"}], ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "20."}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", "am", ",",
      " ", "dm", ",", " ", "dcl", ",", " ", "ssm", ",", " ", "ssc", ",", " ", 
     "sm", ",", " ", "sc", ",", " ", "dE", ",", " ", "dM", ",", " ", "dC"}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"am", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "mm"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "mm"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "gam"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{"dm", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"gam", "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"6", " ", "mm", " ", "kT"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", "0."}], 
         "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "gam", " ", "mm", " ", "kT"}]}], "}"}]}], 
       "}"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"dcl", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"4", " ", "gam", " ", "mm", " ", "kT"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
    ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"ssm", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"LyapunovSolve", "[", 
      RowBox[{"am", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "dm"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ssc", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"LyapunovSolve", "[", 
      RowBox[{"am", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "dcl"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"sm", "[", "t_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"e", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
          RowBox[{"am", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ssm", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"e", " ", ".", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"sys0", " ", "-", " ", "ssm"}], ")"}], " ", ".", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "e", "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"sc", "[", "t_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"e", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
          RowBox[{"am", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ssc", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"e", " ", ".", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"sys0", " ", "-", " ", "ssc"}], ")"}], " ", ".", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "e", "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"dE", "[", 
      RowBox[{"t_", "?", "NumericQ"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
       RowBox[{"sig", "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"dM", "[", 
      RowBox[{"t_", "?", "NumericQ"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
       RowBox[{"sm", "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"dC", "[", 
      RowBox[{"t_", "?", "NumericQ"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
       RowBox[{"sc", "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"dC", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dM", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dE", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0.2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0.2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "0.004"}], ",", " ", "0.03"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", 
      "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"Red", ",", " ", "Thick"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"Blue", ",", " ", "Thick"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"Black", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<t\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<det \[Sigma](t) - \[HBar]^2/4\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
      "   ", 
      RowBox[{
      "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
       " ", "\"\<Only Caldeira-Leggett pierces the floor; this work tracks \
the exact dynamics\>\""}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Placed", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          
          RowBox[{"\"\<Caldeira-Leggett (D_XX = 0)\>\"", ",", 
           " ", "\"\<This work\>\"", ",", 
           " ", "\"\<Exact (Hu-Paz-Zhang)\>\""}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Below"}], 
        "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"Dashed", ",", " ", "Gray", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"0.2", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n",
          "     ", 
         RowBox[{"Inset", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"dC", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"dM", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"dE", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "35"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"{", "Red", "}"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", "Blue", "}"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"Black", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",",
              "\n", "        ", 
             RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "190"}], ",", "\n", 
             "        ", 
             RowBox[{"PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Style", "[", 
               RowBox[{"\"\<full range: all thermalize\>\"", ",", " ", "8"}], 
               "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Scaled", "[", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"0.73", ",", " ", "0.34"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
        "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "580"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[50]:= ",
 CellID->2120100675,ExpressionUUID->"7ba8138a-66ce-478c-2957-8ad4137b2dd6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This work tracks the exact curve closely, the two differing most in the \
initial transient, where the constant-coefficient generator switches on its \
full diffusion at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35c9e6d4-f3c4-84c1-63f6-ff918676ee2b"],
 " while the exact dynamics ramps its up. Over the trajectory the \
constant-coefficient covariance follows the exact one to about a percent, the \
deviation living in that initial slip, the one regime a Markovian description \
is not meant to capture."
}], "Text",
 CellID->950326543,ExpressionUUID->"6fd66644-13e4-6fa7-15ee-782ea591358d"],

Cell["\<\
That leaves the equilibrium, and there the two genuinely differ. Average the \
exact covariance over a late window to strip the ringing, and compare the \
settled variances to the bare Gibbs values and to this work's steady state:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1689126594,ExpressionUUID->"00abf1cf-696b-3507-30a8-e8a9081f9c6d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"mm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"w0", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "10"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"kT", " ", "=", " ", "5."}], ",", " ", "gibbs", ",", " ", "avg", 
     ",", " ", "am", ",", " ", "dm", ",", " ", "ssm"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
   "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"gibbs", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Coth", "[", 
       RowBox[{"w0", "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "kT"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "w0"}], ")"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"avg", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Mean", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Diagonal", "[", 
         RowBox[{"sig", "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "28", ",", " ", "38", ",", " ", "0.2"}], 
         "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"am", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "mm"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "mm"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "gam"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"dm", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"gam", "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"6", " ", "mm", " ", "kT"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", "0."}], 
         "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "gam", " ", "mm", " ", "kT"}]}], "}"}]}], 
       "}"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"ssm", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"LyapunovSolve", "[", 
      RowBox[{"am", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "dm"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"Grid", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Chop", "@", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          
          RowBox[{"\"\<\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\[Sigma]XX\>\"", ",", 
           " ", "\"\<\[Sigma]PP\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<exact (averaged)\>\"", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"avg", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"avg", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          
          RowBox[{"\"\<bare Gibbs\>\"", ",", " ", "gibbs", ",", " ", 
           "gibbs"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<this work steady\>\"", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ssm", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ssm", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Alignment", " ", "->", " ", "Left"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[51]:= ",
 CellID->1490757098,ExpressionUUID->"03d898fe-d35a-9eef-31e7-11bbe6ece435"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The exact position variance settles onto the bare Gibbs value, to the \
precision the averaging affords, which validates the microscopic construction \
against a known closed form. The exact momentum variance, though, sits about \
a percent above it, robustly across sub-windows: the finite-coupling \
mean-force enhancement, the shift of the true equilibrium away from the bare \
Gibbs state when the system is coupled to the bath at finite strength. The \
constant-coefficient generator, pinned to the bare Gibbs value plus its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03dda600-4b0b-c3af-31e2-386a6ebf91f5"],
 " correction, does not carry this ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4de38b79-ee67-8bee-7b90-23228b13d934"],
 " shift, so at equilibrium it and the exact dynamics agree only to the order \
of the coupling. That gap is the honest edge of the surrogate: the \
constant-coefficient generator is faithful to Hu-Paz-Zhang through the \
transient and positive where Caldeira-Leggett is not, but it is a memoryless \
stand-in, not the exact dynamics, and the mean-force shift is what a \
memoryless generator tied to the bare Gibbs state must leave on the table."
}], "Text",
 CellID->148290444,ExpressionUUID->"347cf1ed-0cc4-b4dc-5c03-e8b7a5761e26"],

Cell["Where This Leaves Us (and What Comes Next)", "Section",
 CellID->1707667820,ExpressionUUID->"7d81b9ce-3a4c-aa2a-2bbe-30a8bffef970"],

Cell["\<\
Before closing, let us summarize the most important points we computed and \
verified:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->933399197,ExpressionUUID->"6bb9b374-9caf-337d-1946-2b3e155b9e47"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Ohmic Feynman-Vernon kernel is a hyperbolic-cosecant-squared profile of \
width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["B", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c340229-13f4-0181-15cb-a473a58153eb"],
 ", obtained here as the second derivative of the thermal primitive ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", 
   StyleBox["coth",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Pi]", 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "-", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25dfa134-0866-9bb5-53e4-397ea910e99f"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->955179929,ExpressionUUID->"425139cc-45a5-cefb-726e-b0966c5194c1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "White noise keeps only the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "/", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d922994-f334-45bb-7ba1-c0d186c12f81"],
 " term of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["coth",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "/", "2"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06c25578-1780-b25e-2ef2-4d22a23a00a4"],
 "; the discarded ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "/", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f70617e-b140-9f95-0500-793bc0fae5ff"],
 " term is the whole correction, and its weight is fixed by the single moment \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[Infinity]",
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sinh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], "/", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79d0371a-30a6-04e5-2fef-af4441536ecf"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->775067320,ExpressionUUID->"7d950d76-dd18-2b24-2baa-a533d4ad760e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The kernel is only meaningful as a tempered distribution: the bare ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["sinh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "2"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7234a9f4-3232-6781-23cb-40be47c74deb"],
 " integral diverges at the origin, and the subtraction ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "42668d78-f434-72a4-721d-2525fdc1408e"],
 " is the regularization that makes it finite."
}], "Item",
 CellID->72268088,ExpressionUUID->"0c7cc198-0ad8-2426-3403-d8c2af528f0c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Keeping one term past white noise adds a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69698b1d-3dc2-3628-1f16-2347b4749d72"],
 " piece to the kernel, hence a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "701e1eb7-eeba-61c8-2025-97f08b4f3312"],
 " double commutator with position-diffusion coefficient ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"6", 
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0e322415-281a-3695-37c1-be5f49ac9cff"],
 " to the master equation."
}], "Item",
 CellID->546416532,ExpressionUUID->"61beb272-ef15-9663-1745-343f8aa1fd49"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], "1"], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e8a6a96-06b4-6465-0689-83d0b3414f4f"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], "2"], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55951090-ef25-ccfd-03aa-89dd8ad196c7"],
 ", the Kossakowski determinant is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"3", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "53a2ca13-da2c-324e-0151-ec5cdfde8094"],
 " for this work and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5930221d-821b-4026-08cf-c44737ae130c"],
 " for standard Caldeira-Leggett: the correction is exactly what turns a \
non-positive generator into a Lindblad one, and the corrected generator \
contains no cutoff ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76ba63e9-5df8-c241-1e5a-7ab3547290ab"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->2117784656,ExpressionUUID->"319e51f9-a9ce-1d21-67a6-48a2c87b640b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a harmonic potential the master equation is a Lyapunov flow whose \
steady state is the classical thermal covariance plus ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26f4962c-805e-a216-4e8b-087631e8f17c"],
 " corrections, and a position-squeezed state that pierces the Robertson-Schr\
\[ODoubleDot]dinger floor under Caldeira-Leggett stays above it under this \
work."
}], "Item",
 CellID->853117843,ExpressionUUID->"313d5a7b-7caf-7acc-60c3-5c25755a4816"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Continued past ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2da78195-91be-94f0-5b5c-18df2048feda"],
 ", the fluctuation-path expansion has coefficients weighted by the Bernoulli \
numbers, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "=", "4", 
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "1"}]], "/", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39c6b7ab-78e0-e73c-6ffd-2ef5789aca06"],
 ", and the even-derivative tower ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f7d0c35-7157-44bf-6502-a67f00e22e85"],
 " resums to the exact Ohmic weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["coth",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "/", "2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47b49f91-c3c7-4deb-6d4b-16daf6721731"],
 ": the local expansion is the high-temperature expansion of the exact \
colored-noise spectrum."
}], "Item",
 CellID->623836386,ExpressionUUID->"064e3005-d89e-7c03-2e75-aa6ed92b4769"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Past ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76c2caed-aea0-13a2-1ef1-e3b6cb556188"],
 " the generator's operator content is potential-dependent, because the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "260c3025-1fa9-9acd-4e33-a98f9a5de817"],
 " term carries the acceleration ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b1e6c2c-0452-4134-7925-8676ade7101e"],
 " under the system Hamiltonian: it vanishes for a free particle, where the \
two-operator form is exact to all orders; it renormalizes the coefficients \
for a harmonic potential; and it becomes a genuinely new Lindblad operator \
for an anharmonic well."
}], "Item",
 CellID->564394165,ExpressionUUID->"2982aea8-af87-65d7-5fb1-47f5ca324f3d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Complete positivity is special to the two-term order: the channel variances \
alternate in sign with the Bernoulli numbers, so the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19ac3a5e-0cd6-873c-4f53-bc18a560ea06"],
 " channel is anti-diffusive (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], "4"], "<", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e8690e9-968f-68b3-16bd-09b3233a3a99"],
 ") and its truncation is not completely positive; positivity is restored \
only by the full resummation to a manifestly non-negative spectrum."
}], "Item",
 CellID->2048244887,ExpressionUUID->"2b6bc1ec-c569-bd9f-5968-d8c9ec1d07e5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the harmonic oscillator each further term deepens the match to the \
Gibbs covariance by one power of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25f1a39a-81e0-db80-538e-3ac4379aa9ea"],
 " (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35466be2-b7a8-26dc-637d-82cfc2428c26"],
 " matches ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58bdea72-0ba3-5f4c-0842-0c3cae562596"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e8cef58-e908-949c-16b3-070588a2fee6"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0abc4047-6c7b-4886-3a44-5a21050e1aec"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "4"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "24e21d63-fe6b-5877-4c91-954cfb1e2b5d"],
 "), and the expansion converges only for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[GreaterTilde]", "\[HBar]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"], "/", "2", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "348d2737-4aeb-e3cb-5cb2-bf716e9fb111"],
 ", the first Matsubara frequency, below which the bath memory is genuinely \
non-Markovian."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1432457359,ExpressionUUID->"2161c865-0900-0907-571e-e24fa8b5586d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Benchmarked against the exact reduced dynamics of the microscopic model \
(the Hu-Paz-Zhang dynamics, computed by discretizing the bath), the \
constant-coefficient generator is a faithful memoryless surrogate: it tracks \
the exact covariance to about a percent through the transient and never \
pierces the uncertainty floor that Caldeira-Leggett does. It is a stand-in, \
not the exact dynamics, in two honest ways: it fixes positivity differently \
(a constant position diffusion, where the exact dynamics carries a \
time-dependent anomalous cross and no position diffusion), and at equilibrium \
it misses the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3cadbe4b-a339-c651-6452-3014d6cdacbb"],
 " mean-force enhancement of the momentum variance, because it is pinned to \
the bare Gibbs state."
}], "Item",
 CellID->200346680,ExpressionUUID->"31169419-f57b-983b-672d-0e42fc0feb01"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "You now have a complete, computation-first toolkit for the corrected \
high-temperature limit of quantum Brownian motion: the kernel algebra from \
primitives, the distributional regularization done honestly, the Kossakowski \
matrix and its spectrum as the positivity test, the covariance flow as the \
physical picture, the systematic expansion that settles the operator \
structure, positivity, and temperature reach of the higher orders in closed \
form, and the exact microscopic benchmark that weighs the whole construction \
against the dynamics it approximates. The natural continuations are the \
anharmonic generator on a position grid, where the new ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40aa99e8-53bd-499c-70a9-10b266481be6"],
 " operator and the loss of a finite Lindblad form show up directly in the \
density matrix, and the stochastic unraveling of the generator into a \
Schrodinger equation with a momentum-coupled noise, where the two-term \
generator's new piece appears as a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d165407-aaf3-867b-0b2e-4e60ce87ed41"],
 " coupling. The two-term generator keeps the invariant we leaned on \
throughout, that nothing in it depends on the cutoff ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75cb8946-a0dc-0da7-23c8-2123d169578d"],
 "; the systematic expansion shows the price of going further is a return of \
the potential and, eventually, of the memory."
}], "Text",
 CellID->447384324,ExpressionUUID->"63688a50-35e7-99e6-1117-2c1a4393ebcc"],

Cell["Acknowledgment", "Subsection",
 CellID->1438124241,ExpressionUUID->"12187c95-2034-8b29-4238-75df51c6d673"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook follows the derivation of Pleasance, Aurell, and Petruccione, \
\"High-temperature limit penalizing high-frequency quantum fluctuations\" \
(arXiv:2508.14262), and reproduces its central results as live computations. \
Any errors in the reconstruction are mine.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2000382747,ExpressionUUID->"34b193bd-0a67-a7a6-5c4e-0ae7af130d8c"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (February 17, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"4fca8ec2-4b73-3b52-75c9-27ac6e0789b8"
]
